304
00:13:11.310 --> 00:13:12.830
Lice Fast Facts.

305
00:13:13.530 --> 00:13:16.670
One, lice-like clean scalps.

306
00:13:17.990 --> 00:13:18.910
Clean scalps.

307
00:13:19.030 --> 00:13:19.310
Yes.

308
00:13:19.630 --> 00:13:24.390
So in this episode, we're assuming that it was like, oh, Meredith never bathes.

309
00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:24.630
Right.

310
00:13:24.630 --> 00:13:25.490
That's why she has lice.

311
00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:26.010
No, no, no.

312
00:13:26.210 --> 00:13:27.510
Lice-like a clean scalp.

313
00:13:27.730 --> 00:13:27.870
Yeah.

314
00:13:28.190 --> 00:13:30.870
Greasy scalp they, like, slide off of or something.

315
00:13:31.130 --> 00:13:31.490
Oh.

316
00:13:31.730 --> 00:13:32.730
I mean, I don't know.

317
00:13:33.050 --> 00:13:37.290
I'm just, like, imagining little lice just, like, sliding off people's heads.

318
00:13:37.290 --> 00:13:41.730
Number two, lice cannot fly or jump.

319
00:13:42.090 --> 00:13:44.250
You have to really be close to someone.

320
00:13:44.650 --> 00:13:47.990
Lice have to, like, crawl into another person's head.

321
00:13:48.230 --> 00:13:48.370
Yeah.

322
00:13:48.810 --> 00:13:49.030
Okay.

323
00:13:49.410 --> 00:13:50.450
Laurel said gross.

324
00:13:50.910 --> 00:13:51.750
Yeah, that is gross.

325
00:13:52.170 --> 00:13:55.730
Number three, they can only infest your head.

326
00:13:56.570 --> 00:14:02.570
They can live in bedding, a rug, clothing, or fabric, but only for 24 hours.

327
00:14:02.930 --> 00:14:06.090
And lice cannot reproduce off the head.

328
00:14:06.590 --> 00:14:12.770
So if they get transferred to a hat, they can't multiply unless they get back on a head.

329
00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:13.590
So gross.

330
00:14:14.090 --> 00:14:14.390
Mm-hmm.

331
00:14:14.390 --> 00:14:20.930
Also, I guess Meredith really didn't need to wax her pubic area for lice.

332
00:14:21.390 --> 00:14:22.890
She didn't want it to travel south.

333
00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:25.310
Here is lice fact number four.

334
00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:29.130
Have you heard of the blood rhesus factor?

335
00:14:29.470 --> 00:14:35.470
That's, like, where your blood type can determine certain things, like, I don't know.

336
00:14:35.470 --> 00:14:44.070
I've heard of it loosely, but I guess it's true that lice prefer positive blood over negative blood types.

337
00:14:44.750 --> 00:14:46.850
But they will feed on either.

338
00:14:47.490 --> 00:14:53.390
However, lice can't, like, start on one blood type and move to another blood type.

339
00:14:53.570 --> 00:15:03.190
So if a louse is feeding on a person with A positive blood and then they end up getting transferred to a person with B negative blood, it won't live.

340
00:15:03.550 --> 00:15:05.530
That is fascinating.

341
00:15:05.810 --> 00:15:05.970
Right?

342
00:15:06.270 --> 00:15:06.750
Yeah.

343
00:15:07.370 --> 00:15:07.710
Laurel.

344
00:15:07.710 --> 00:15:08.070
Laurel.

345
00:15:08.230 --> 00:15:09.450
Way to go, Laurel.

346
00:15:09.550 --> 00:15:10.050
I know.

347
00:15:10.050 --> 00:15:20.510
Laurel said this proved true in my family because she said only the people with negative blood had lice and the people with positive blood did not get lice in her family.

348
00:15:20.870 --> 00:15:21.670
Oh, man.

349
00:15:21.950 --> 00:15:23.190
This is so interesting.

350
00:15:23.750 --> 00:15:25.370
Lice fact number five.

351
00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:33.130
You do not have to wash everything in your house like Pam did because lice cannot actually infest your whole house.

352
00:15:33.130 --> 00:15:43.150
You just have to wash your bed linens, any recently worn clothing, and put any, like, hair items like brushes, combs in the freezer, and that's it.

353
00:15:43.330 --> 00:15:51.910
However, Laurel does recommend buying something called the Terminator comb, which is the only comb that will really rid your head of lice.

354
00:15:52.670 --> 00:16:02.150
And finally, Laurel says, as the lady was checking my 12-year-old's head and she was watching the lice episode, Dwight has the line,

355
00:16:02.290 --> 00:16:07.790
I wash my hair every day with lice shampoo, and the lady looked at us and said, no, do not ever do that.

356
00:16:08.170 --> 00:16:10.550
Do not wash your hair with lice shampoo every day.

357
00:16:12.030 --> 00:16:16.110
And then Laurel says, and now you know more about lice than you ever thought you'd know.

358
00:16:16.750 --> 00:16:17.830
Well done, Laurel.

359
00:16:17.950 --> 00:16:18.390
Laurel.

360
00:16:18.630 --> 00:16:19.490
Well done.

361
00:16:19.750 --> 00:16:21.550
This was, I don't even know what to say.

362
00:16:21.550 --> 00:16:22.230
Hey, I'm speechless.

363
00:16:22.470 --> 00:16:23.690
You have out-deep-dived me.

364
00:16:23.910 --> 00:16:24.530
I love it.

365
00:16:24.910 --> 00:16:28.630
I mean, not that I'm the deep-dive expert, but wow, you really covered it.

366
00:16:28.730 --> 00:16:29.610
You did a great job.

367
00:16:29.730 --> 00:16:29.970
Yes.

