And everyone gets a cold bug because the weather swings.

510
00:21:25.560 --> 00:21:26.020
So extreme.

511
00:21:26.020 --> 00:21:26.440
Temperature.

512
00:21:26.640 --> 00:21:26.700
Yeah.

513
00:21:26.860 --> 00:21:26.920
Yeah.

514
00:21:27.640 --> 00:21:34.540
Also, on the very first day of filming, they scheduled a test of the bald cap slash shaving rig with Kate,

515
00:21:34.760 --> 00:21:40.080
but we did not film that scene when she shaves her head until the final day on Friday.

516
00:21:40.700 --> 00:21:43.340
And then, you know, they love to decorate our call sheets.

517
00:21:43.500 --> 00:21:49.080
And on Tuesday, the call sheets had little American flags and balloons and a bald eagle

518
00:21:49.080 --> 00:21:52.140
because it was Super Tuesday and everyone was voting.

519
00:21:52.480 --> 00:21:54.200
Lady, it's Super Tuesday today.

520
00:21:54.380 --> 00:21:54.880
I know.

521
00:21:54.880 --> 00:21:56.640
We're recording this on Super Tuesday.

522
00:21:56.880 --> 00:21:57.300
I know.

523
00:21:57.740 --> 00:21:58.540
That's so crazy.

524
00:21:58.800 --> 00:21:59.320
Isn't that crazy?

525
00:21:59.480 --> 00:21:59.740
Yeah.

526
00:22:00.400 --> 00:22:01.520
Are we in the Matrix?

527
00:22:02.100 --> 00:22:03.060
I don't know.

528
00:22:04.440 --> 00:22:08.780
I'm wearing a Joshua Tree sweatshirt that I didn't even think about, and you're going there?

529
00:22:08.840 --> 00:22:09.660
What's happening?

530
00:22:09.800 --> 00:22:10.340
What's happening?

531
00:22:10.460 --> 00:22:11.680
The coincidences today.

532
00:22:11.860 --> 00:22:12.180
Mm-hmm.

533
00:22:12.500 --> 00:22:13.960
Let's hope no one gets lice.

534
00:22:14.260 --> 00:22:15.540
There's a glitch in the Matrix.

535
00:22:15.540 --> 00:22:16.200
I don't know.

536
00:22:16.640 --> 00:22:20.760
Well, listen, this episode is going to open with a little scene in the break room.

537
00:22:21.000 --> 00:22:23.300
It's just Jim and Daryl and Kevin,

538
00:22:23.300 --> 00:22:25.520
and they're kind of arguing about basketball,

539
00:22:25.520 --> 00:22:28.380
and Jim keeps biting his lip.

540
00:22:28.660 --> 00:22:30.600
Oh, and he does that thing that you do.

541
00:22:30.720 --> 00:22:32.880
You know when you bite your lip, and then it makes a bump,

542
00:22:32.960 --> 00:22:35.000
and then you keep biting the bump.

543
00:22:35.140 --> 00:22:36.060
You bite the bump.

544
00:22:36.480 --> 00:22:36.720
Ugh.

545
00:22:37.040 --> 00:22:39.580
Did you notice Jim John's baby carrots?

546
00:22:39.840 --> 00:22:40.400
I sure did.

547
00:22:40.400 --> 00:22:45.160
I called them Jim John's baby carrots because it's really John that likes to eat the baby carrots

548
00:22:45.160 --> 00:22:45.780
as Jim.

549
00:22:45.960 --> 00:22:46.660
Jim John.

550
00:22:46.800 --> 00:22:48.100
Jim John's baby carrots.

551
00:22:48.560 --> 00:22:50.860
Angela, we got a fan question for you.

552
00:22:51.220 --> 00:22:51.620
Mm-hmm.

553
00:22:52.020 --> 00:22:52.880
From Lee M.

554
00:22:53.000 --> 00:22:53.740
in San Jose.

555
00:22:53.740 --> 00:22:58.480
On the Blu-ray for this episode, there is a deleted scene for a cold open

556
00:22:58.480 --> 00:23:02.040
where the group discovers Creed's map to the office.

557
00:23:02.300 --> 00:23:04.880
Was this shot as an alternate cold open,

558
00:23:04.880 --> 00:23:08.940
or was the cold open where Jim bites his lip planned for another episode?

559
00:23:08.940 --> 00:23:09.740
What's going on?

560
00:23:10.040 --> 00:23:10.740
All right, Lee.

561
00:23:10.900 --> 00:23:12.420
I have all the answers for you.

562
00:23:12.760 --> 00:23:17.480
So Jim biting his tongue was originally the cold open for Dwight's Christmas.

563
00:23:18.260 --> 00:23:18.760
Oh.

564
00:23:19.300 --> 00:23:19.540
Yeah.

565
00:23:19.780 --> 00:23:20.580
Remember when we—

566
00:23:20.580 --> 00:23:22.140
Sorry, my mouth is full of cake.

567
00:23:23.160 --> 00:23:26.540
Oh, yes, but then Dwight's Christmas has no cold open, no credits.

568
00:23:26.800 --> 00:23:27.000
Right.

569
00:23:27.160 --> 00:23:28.640
You commented on that right away.

570
00:23:28.760 --> 00:23:30.420
You're like, did you notice there's no cold open?

571
00:23:30.580 --> 00:23:31.100
There was.

572
00:23:31.200 --> 00:23:32.260
They just didn't include it.

573
00:23:32.400 --> 00:23:36.140
And yes, Lee, there's this whole storyline about Creed and his map.

574
00:23:36.620 --> 00:23:37.660
It's really funny.

575
00:23:37.660 --> 00:23:41.120
It was cut, but I guess you can still see it in the deleted scenes on the DVD

576
00:23:41.120 --> 00:23:42.900
and on the Blu-ray disc.

577
00:23:43.240 --> 00:23:46.140
Here's how it read in the shooting draft, and it was the cold open.

578
00:23:47.180 --> 00:23:48.540
Interior break room day.

579
00:23:48.760 --> 00:23:54.440
Daryl, Pam, Phyllis, Oscar, and Toby are gathered around a large piece of paper on the break room table.

580
00:23:54.820 --> 00:23:56.380
There's a secretive vibe.

581
00:23:56.700 --> 00:23:58.360
The camera pushes in on the paper.

582
00:23:58.600 --> 00:24:00.240
It's a hand-drawn map.

583
00:24:00.420 --> 00:24:01.880
The group all look at the map.

584
00:24:02.040 --> 00:24:04.960
Daryl says, maybe it's a shopping list?

585
00:24:05.160 --> 00:24:09.560
Phyllis says, but what, he's buying a ham, a skeleton, and a mustache?

586
00:24:10.260 --> 00:24:11.240
A mustache.

587
00:24:11.660 --> 00:24:12.220
A mustache.

588
00:24:12.620 --> 00:24:14.220
Daryl says, it's Creed.

589
00:24:14.220 --> 00:24:14.340
Creed.

590
00:24:14.500 --> 00:24:20.700
And then Pam has a talking head, and she says, we found this weird drawing under Creed's desk.

591
00:24:21.000 --> 00:24:22.500
She shows us the drawing.

592
00:24:22.720 --> 00:24:23.920
There are waves.

593
00:24:24.160 --> 00:24:29.540
There's a bucket, a skeleton, a ham, straight lines separating them.

594
00:24:29.760 --> 00:24:32.040
It's a very simple maze.

595
00:24:32.200 --> 00:24:34.080
A few X's and some arrows.

596
00:24:34.080 --> 00:24:35.820
Pam goes, bizarre, huh?

597
00:24:36.000 --> 00:24:42.280
She shows the diagram to camera, then looks at it and turns it 90 degrees and goes, oh, my God.

598
00:24:42.700 --> 00:24:48.340
Pam bursts back into the break room where the previous group are still lounging and says, it's a map.

599
00:24:48.520 --> 00:24:50.160
And they all say, what?

600
00:24:50.420 --> 00:24:53.400
And then they all figure out who they are on the map.

601
00:24:53.540 --> 00:24:54.700
It's really funny.

602
00:24:54.700 --> 00:24:59.580
So it's like a map of the office, and then all the people are represented on the map.

603
00:25:00.180 --> 00:25:01.740
Angela is the skeleton.

604
00:25:03.400 --> 00:25:05.040
And Toby is the toilet.

605
00:25:05.860 --> 00:25:06.280
Wow.

606
00:25:06.680 --> 00:25:07.840
Daryl is a cheeseburger.

607
00:25:08.220 --> 00:25:08.640
Wow.

608
00:25:08.860 --> 00:25:09.240
I know.

609
00:25:09.580 --> 00:25:11.060
But it is on the DVDs.

610
00:25:11.120 --> 00:25:12.020
So there you go, Lee.

611
00:25:12.480 --> 00:25:12.920
Amazing.

612
00:25:13.240 --> 00:25:14.000
Great question.

613
00:25:14.100 --> 00:25:14.600
Great answer.

614
00:25:14.980 --> 00:25:17.360
So this is how the episode actually starts.

615
00:25:17.640 --> 00:25:19.480
A person comes into the office.

616
00:25:19.480 --> 00:25:20.260
They're in a coat.

617
00:25:20.380 --> 00:25:21.920
They have a hat kind of pulled down.

618
00:25:21.920 --> 00:25:23.620
They look a little ragged.

619
00:25:23.740 --> 00:25:25.560
And Aaron says, oh, good morning, Meredith.

620
00:25:25.860 --> 00:25:27.100
And it's Pam.

621
00:25:27.520 --> 00:25:28.240
It's Pam.

622
00:25:28.520 --> 00:25:29.000
Yeah.

623
00:25:29.200 --> 00:25:34.040
There's a talking head where Pam reveals that Jim has been spending a few nights a week in

624
00:25:34.040 --> 00:25:36.280
Philly, and it's been challenging.

625
00:25:36.980 --> 00:25:42.140
And we see a montage of Pam sort of trying to take out the trash, and things are falling

626
00:25:42.140 --> 00:25:42.540
everywhere.

627
00:25:42.800 --> 00:25:48.180
And then she shares that her current problem is that Cece has lice, and she was up all

628
00:25:48.180 --> 00:25:48.520
night.

629
00:25:48.780 --> 00:25:49.240
Yeah.

630
00:25:49.300 --> 00:25:51.140
She was disinfecting the entire house.

631
00:25:51.140 --> 00:25:52.860
And then she says, don't tell Jim.

632
00:25:53.000 --> 00:25:55.940
He has a really big meeting today, and he's doing it for the family.

633
00:25:56.100 --> 00:25:57.680
Like, she doesn't want to stress him out with this.

634
00:25:57.840 --> 00:25:58.080
Mm-hmm.

635
00:25:58.760 --> 00:26:01.080
Lady, we got fan mail.

636
00:26:01.400 --> 00:26:02.020
Oh, yeah.

637
00:26:03.240 --> 00:26:06.120
Very passionate fan mail from Aaron S.

638
00:26:06.400 --> 00:26:07.600
in Baltimore, Maryland.

639
00:26:07.900 --> 00:26:09.440
Here is what Aaron had to say.

640
00:26:09.940 --> 00:26:10.400
Years.

641
00:26:11.000 --> 00:26:15.860
I have waited years to finally get up on my soapbox about this episode.

642
00:26:16.280 --> 00:26:17.100
Oh, wow.

643
00:26:17.220 --> 00:26:17.880
Let's hear it.

644
00:26:17.960 --> 00:26:18.280
I know.

645
00:26:18.400 --> 00:26:19.620
Aaron's coming in hot, huh?

646
00:26:19.620 --> 00:26:21.140
Yeah, she's hot to trot.

647
00:26:21.420 --> 00:26:22.160
She is.

648
00:26:22.380 --> 00:26:24.020
Here's what she goes on to say.

649
00:26:24.280 --> 00:26:30.660
While I have plenty of thoughts on the entire Jim Philly storyline, my biggest peccadillo

650
00:26:30.660 --> 00:26:34.960
about the whole thing is how Pam is portrayed in this episode.

651
00:26:35.260 --> 00:26:39.560
Pam is a strong, independent woman, a mother of two, a professional.

652
00:26:39.860 --> 00:26:43.260
She is fully capable of caring for her children on her own.

653
00:26:43.440 --> 00:26:46.240
She did just fine while Jim was in Tallahassee.

654
00:26:46.240 --> 00:26:49.200
Do you like the tone I'm taking to read the letter?

655
00:26:49.300 --> 00:26:49.640
I do.

656
00:26:49.840 --> 00:26:50.580
It's a picadillo.

657
00:26:50.860 --> 00:26:51.640
It's a picadillo.

658
00:26:52.800 --> 00:26:53.720
I'll go on.

659
00:26:54.220 --> 00:26:59.880
Pam and Jim both work full-time, so her children obviously have a well-established daycare situation

660
00:26:59.880 --> 00:27:03.120
going on, and her mother is staying with her to help.

661
00:27:03.120 --> 00:27:08.520
The idea that she would be so overwhelmed by being home alone with her children for a few

662
00:27:08.520 --> 00:27:14.240
days that she would show up to work with unbrushed hair and a mist-buttoned sweater is just insulting

663
00:27:14.240 --> 00:27:19.080
to moms everywhere who routinely hold down the fort with grace and panache.

664
00:27:19.080 --> 00:27:21.500
A picadillo and a panache.

665
00:27:21.660 --> 00:27:22.980
I'm telling you, Erin.

666
00:27:23.180 --> 00:27:25.780
Erin, this is your soapbox moment.

667
00:27:25.780 --> 00:27:26.600
This is it.

668
00:27:26.680 --> 00:27:28.740
I'm doing my best to give it all I got, too.

669
00:27:29.160 --> 00:27:29.820
There's more.

670
00:27:30.240 --> 00:27:31.140
Erin says,

671
00:27:31.780 --> 00:27:37.240
Sure, she would be more tired, and Lice throws a wrench in the gears, but I cannot imagine any

672
00:27:37.240 --> 00:27:41.480
mother anywhere showing up to work like that no matter how rough their night was.

673
00:27:41.480 --> 00:27:47.020
After all the personal growth we've seen in Pam over the years, I just hated to see her

674
00:27:47.020 --> 00:27:49.820
presented as so helpless without her husband.

675
00:27:50.140 --> 00:27:52.500
And then Erin signs off by saying,

676
00:27:52.780 --> 00:27:54.200
Dismounts Soapbox.

677
00:27:54.880 --> 00:27:58.120
Sets aside for Angela in a few episodes.

678
00:27:58.420 --> 00:27:58.820
Oh!

679
00:27:59.140 --> 00:28:01.400
So, Erin, I'll be looking for that letter.

680
00:28:01.600 --> 00:28:03.800
I have a feeling I know which episode, too.

681
00:28:04.300 --> 00:28:08.060
We got another letter that I'm calling Counterpoint.

682
00:28:08.320 --> 00:28:08.680
Oh.

683
00:28:08.680 --> 00:28:10.920
This is from Kiana R.

684
00:28:11.080 --> 00:28:12.740
in Williams, Georgia, who said,

685
00:28:12.900 --> 00:28:16.960
When my husband leaves me with the kids for several days, I feel like I'm going to die.

686
00:28:17.220 --> 00:28:17.660
LOL.

687
00:28:18.460 --> 00:28:23.460
I felt you portrayed so well the exhausted desperation of a mother doing it all on her

688
00:28:23.460 --> 00:28:25.360
own when she normally has help.

689
00:28:25.920 --> 00:28:28.020
Well, Angela, I thought I'd open it up.

690
00:28:28.140 --> 00:28:29.160
What do we think?

691
00:28:29.540 --> 00:28:30.680
Are we with Erin?

692
00:28:31.040 --> 00:28:32.360
Are we with Kiana?

693
00:28:32.680 --> 00:28:33.820
Are we somewhere in the middle?

694
00:28:34.040 --> 00:28:34.640
Where are we?

695
00:28:35.260 --> 00:28:39.020
I mean, listen, I think I'm with Erin.

696
00:28:39.740 --> 00:28:40.660
You're with Erin.

697
00:28:40.820 --> 00:28:41.520
I'm with Erin.

698
00:28:41.860 --> 00:28:46.660
I mean, you know, I was a single mom for a few years, and I had to get s**t done.

699
00:28:46.880 --> 00:28:47.100
Yeah.

700
00:28:47.720 --> 00:28:51.180
I might not have had the cutest hairdo when I showed up to work,

701
00:28:51.900 --> 00:28:54.740
but I still showed up and I had everything done.

702
00:28:54.940 --> 00:28:55.260
Mm-hmm.

703
00:28:55.520 --> 00:28:58.540
So I guess I also do really hear Kiana, too.

704
00:28:58.540 --> 00:29:04.860
I mean, I probably didn't look super put together, but I was able to take out the trash

705
00:29:04.860 --> 00:29:06.460
without spilling it into the street.

706
00:29:06.620 --> 00:29:07.100
Whatever.

707
00:29:07.480 --> 00:29:09.500
That moment was ridiculous to me.

708
00:29:09.600 --> 00:29:14.140
I'm like, Pam can put the trash bin on the street without tipping it over.

709
00:29:14.360 --> 00:29:15.780
She's not that tired.

710
00:29:16.100 --> 00:29:21.140
I guess now as I talk it out, I see both sides, but I think I lean more to Erin.

711
00:29:21.420 --> 00:29:22.400
That's very interesting.

712
00:29:22.400 --> 00:29:26.840
I hadn't even considered Erin's point of view on this until I read the letter,

713
00:29:26.840 --> 00:29:32.300
and I saw there was a lot of value in that letter, but I will tell you I am a Kiana.

714
00:29:32.680 --> 00:29:33.700
You are a Kiana.

715
00:29:33.780 --> 00:29:36.260
I completely fall apart when Lee leaves town.

716
00:29:36.880 --> 00:29:40.520
I have been Pam trying to take the trash out, okay?

717
00:29:40.520 --> 00:29:43.920
I don't take the trash out in my family ever, ever.

718
00:29:43.920 --> 00:29:46.200
We have a running joke when my husband goes out of town.

719
00:29:46.320 --> 00:29:51.340
I will send him a photo of our kitchen trash can, like, overflowing, and I'll be like, it's broken.

720
00:29:52.000 --> 00:29:54.020
Usually I throw the trash and it disappears.

721
00:29:54.020 --> 00:29:55.120
I don't know where it goes.

722
00:29:55.260 --> 00:29:57.080
It's always ready for me to use.

723
00:29:57.220 --> 00:30:02.000
Like, the trash can's broken, babe, because he is trash guy.

724
00:30:02.180 --> 00:30:03.920
And there's other things he does, too.

725
00:30:04.100 --> 00:30:07.720
I don't know how we've done this division of labor, almost unspoken.

726
00:30:08.160 --> 00:30:11.220
I mean, as far as he's concerned, the refrigerator cleans itself.

727
00:30:11.460 --> 00:30:14.480
You know, I don't think he's ever thrown out a rotten piece of anything in the fridge.

728
00:30:14.620 --> 00:30:15.040
That's me.

729
00:30:15.200 --> 00:30:16.300
Somehow we have these jobs.

730
00:30:17.100 --> 00:30:18.400
And I don't know.

731
00:30:18.400 --> 00:30:22.740
I have accidentally tried to take two cans to the curb at the same time, and one falls over.

732
00:30:22.920 --> 00:30:24.500
I'm a mess when Lee leaves.

733
00:30:24.500 --> 00:30:25.080
I am.

734
00:30:25.260 --> 00:30:26.900
I'm a grumpy mess.

735
00:30:26.980 --> 00:30:27.800
I'm overwhelmed.

736
00:30:28.220 --> 00:30:29.780
My balance is all off.

737
00:30:29.940 --> 00:30:32.920
You did call me because the lights went out in your house.

738
00:30:33.160 --> 00:30:34.400
And Lee was out of town.

739
00:30:34.400 --> 00:30:36.100
He was skiing with your son.

740
00:30:36.180 --> 00:30:36.420
Yes.

741
00:30:36.440 --> 00:30:37.720
And you were like, Ange, the power went out.

742
00:30:37.780 --> 00:30:39.040
And I was like, okay, well.

743
00:30:39.240 --> 00:30:41.200
I was like, someone needs to know.

744
00:30:41.360 --> 00:30:43.000
I was like, it's all good.

745
00:30:43.160 --> 00:30:44.500
Do you need me to come over?

746
00:30:44.660 --> 00:30:45.500
No, I'm a mess.

747
00:30:45.500 --> 00:30:46.500
I am a mess.

748
00:30:46.840 --> 00:30:51.620
So I guess I felt like Pam was me when Lee goes out of town.

749
00:30:52.100 --> 00:30:55.060
And I try to do what she does, where I try to be like, no, no.

750
00:30:55.260 --> 00:30:56.260
It's all good here.

751
00:30:56.600 --> 00:30:57.880
Nothing to worry about.

752
00:30:58.700 --> 00:31:00.900
I'm not falling apart with trash on the street.

753
00:31:00.900 --> 00:31:01.600
It's all good.

754
00:31:01.780 --> 00:31:04.040
So that was a very honest performance for you.

755
00:31:04.160 --> 00:31:04.980
For me, it was.

756
00:31:05.080 --> 00:31:05.300
Yes.

757
00:31:05.760 --> 00:31:06.980
Yeah, I think I'm more Erin.

758
00:31:07.340 --> 00:31:08.400
You are more Erin.

759
00:31:10.160 --> 00:31:11.960
Jim is now going to have a talking head.

760
00:31:11.960 --> 00:31:16.580
He shares that he's meeting his personal hero today, Dr. J, a.k.a.

761
00:31:16.840 --> 00:31:17.760
Julius Irving.

762
00:31:18.120 --> 00:31:25.440
But he can't rub it in Pam's face because that would be like if he was home with the kids and she was out like go-karting with, I don't know, John Stamos.

763
00:31:26.220 --> 00:31:27.660
That's such a funny line.

764
00:31:27.740 --> 00:31:28.520
It's so specific.

765
00:31:28.820 --> 00:31:30.560
We got a fan question from Ann M.

766
00:31:30.620 --> 00:31:35.340
in Florida who said, go-karting with John Stamos is one of the funniest lines in this episode.

767
00:31:35.640 --> 00:31:37.040
Were there any alts?

768
00:31:37.200 --> 00:31:39.160
I feel like if there were, I'd love to hear.

769
00:31:39.600 --> 00:31:40.420
There were.

770
00:31:40.860 --> 00:31:46.680
Yeah, I mean, I know this was the scripted talking head, but I did not remember that there were alts.

771
00:31:46.820 --> 00:31:49.220
There were a few alts, and I'll share one with you.

772
00:31:49.320 --> 00:31:54.780
So everything is the same except instead of John Stamos, they would just rotate in different names.

773
00:31:54.920 --> 00:31:55.140
Oh.

774
00:31:55.160 --> 00:31:55.820
So here's one.

775
00:31:56.080 --> 00:31:59.500
Jim would have said, this would be like if Pam got to spend the day with Banksy.

776
00:31:59.680 --> 00:32:00.320
I think.

777
00:32:00.440 --> 00:32:01.360
He's a person, right?

778
00:32:01.980 --> 00:32:02.220
Hmm.

779
00:32:02.700 --> 00:32:08.360
Well, I thought that this talking head was very funny because I have another splitting up together story.

780
00:32:08.620 --> 00:32:10.920
I guess that's what this episode is about for me.

781
00:32:10.920 --> 00:32:16.120
When I worked on splitting up together, it was on the lot, the Warner Brothers lot.

782
00:32:16.420 --> 00:32:17.920
It's a huge lot.

783
00:32:18.040 --> 00:32:19.100
It's like a small city.

784
00:32:19.240 --> 00:32:20.280
Very, very big.

785
00:32:20.280 --> 00:32:25.580
And our dressing rooms that we were assigned, there are these buildings with dressing rooMs.

786
00:32:25.740 --> 00:32:27.840
It's very like old Hollywood sort of.

787
00:32:27.920 --> 00:32:29.300
It's like the old studio days.

788
00:32:29.520 --> 00:32:29.860
Yes.

789
00:32:30.460 --> 00:32:30.900
Fascinating.

790
00:32:31.060 --> 00:32:32.340
It was very fun to shoot there.

791
00:32:32.340 --> 00:32:37.340
So our building with our dressing rooms was very far away from our soundstage.

792
00:32:38.560 --> 00:32:44.940
And they would have to drive us around in little golf carts to get us there in a timely manner.

793
00:32:45.240 --> 00:32:48.400
But also there was like a commissary, a restaurant.

794
00:32:48.440 --> 00:32:53.480
There was a little gift shop that my kids would go to, and I would buy them candy if they visited me.

795
00:32:53.680 --> 00:32:55.620
The Sony Studio is the same way.

796
00:32:55.740 --> 00:33:00.980
When I did that show, Your Family Are Mine, it was you and I had never filmed on a big studio lot.

797
00:33:01.060 --> 00:33:01.280
No.

798
00:33:01.280 --> 00:33:03.040
So it was so interesting.

799
00:33:03.280 --> 00:33:04.160
There's like a gym.

800
00:33:04.400 --> 00:33:04.920
Yes.

801
00:33:05.080 --> 00:33:06.740
There's like a little market store.

802
00:33:07.040 --> 00:33:08.520
So I asked,

803
00:33:08.680 --> 00:33:21.120
could I rent a little golf cart for myself and have my own little golf cart so that I could get around and like go to the little coffee place or get myself to set or do these things?

804
00:33:21.300 --> 00:33:23.900
And they said, no.

805
00:33:24.900 --> 00:33:30.320
Actors were prohibited from having their own golf carts or scooters.

806
00:33:30.440 --> 00:33:30.780
Why?

807
00:33:31.280 --> 00:33:32.480
Because of John Stamos.

808
00:33:32.760 --> 00:33:33.000
What?

809
00:33:33.280 --> 00:33:33.740
Yes.

810
00:33:34.160 --> 00:33:34.660
What?

811
00:33:34.800 --> 00:33:35.580
What'd he do?

812
00:33:35.880 --> 00:33:38.580
Like he got everyone banned?

813
00:33:38.880 --> 00:33:39.020
Yes.

814
00:33:39.020 --> 00:33:40.080
All actors banned?

815
00:33:40.080 --> 00:33:40.500
Yes.

816
00:33:40.600 --> 00:33:45.640
And I feel okay telling this story because I ran into him at a party after this.

817
00:33:45.760 --> 00:33:50.140
And I was like, John, you are why I couldn't have a golf cart at Warner Brothers.

818
00:33:50.140 --> 00:33:51.320
And he goes, I know.

819
00:33:51.580 --> 00:33:52.360
I'm so sorry.

820
00:33:52.600 --> 00:33:52.860
What?

821
00:33:53.840 --> 00:33:54.760
I don't know.

822
00:33:54.920 --> 00:33:58.760
I guess they shot Full House there or something or maybe Fuller House.

823
00:33:58.780 --> 00:34:00.080
I'm not sure which one.

824
00:34:00.220 --> 00:34:06.520
But I guess he would zip around in the little golf carts or on the little scooters.

825
00:34:06.520 --> 00:34:08.640
And they were like, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no.

826
00:34:08.640 --> 00:34:18.340
Somehow him zipping around got us all banned from being able to use any mode of like self-transport on the Warner Brothers lot.

827
00:34:18.440 --> 00:34:18.880
Lady.

828
00:34:19.140 --> 00:34:20.440
Just the way he reacted.

829
00:34:20.600 --> 00:34:21.360
Like, I know.

830
00:34:21.360 --> 00:34:23.380
So it's not just for zipping around.

831
00:34:23.560 --> 00:34:24.100
I don't know.

832
00:34:24.220 --> 00:34:24.980
I don't know.

833
00:34:25.100 --> 00:34:27.180
But he was like, I'm so sorry.

834
00:34:27.280 --> 00:34:28.460
I think they were having races.

835
00:34:28.800 --> 00:34:30.460
I bet he tipped one over or something.

836
00:34:30.480 --> 00:34:30.840
Maybe.

837
00:34:31.040 --> 00:34:31.560
I don't know.

838
00:34:31.640 --> 00:34:32.720
I don't know all the details.

839
00:34:33.460 --> 00:34:36.060
Maybe I'll run into him again and I'll get a refresher.

840
00:34:36.220 --> 00:34:37.680
But we had a good laugh about it.

841
00:34:37.780 --> 00:34:41.120
John, we want the full scoop about you getting everyone banned from having golf carts.

842
00:34:41.260 --> 00:34:42.420
On the Warner Brothers lot.

843
00:34:42.580 --> 00:34:50.200
But it made me laugh because, you know, go-karting, golf-karting, just the idea of zipping around with John Stamos, it holds water.

844
00:34:50.200 --> 00:34:51.400
There's some reality there.

845
00:34:51.780 --> 00:34:52.720
He would do that.

846
00:34:52.920 --> 00:34:55.040
Well, this Pam and Jim phone call wraps up.

847
00:34:55.140 --> 00:34:56.360
They both kind of lie to each other.

848
00:34:56.480 --> 00:34:57.760
Like, Pam's like, I'm doing great.

849
00:34:58.020 --> 00:35:00.160
And Jim's like, oh, my taxi's here.

850
00:35:00.240 --> 00:35:01.220
But it's actually a limo.

851
00:35:01.280 --> 00:35:02.180
And he's really excited.

852
00:35:02.200 --> 00:35:03.440
But he's downplaying that.

853
00:35:04.440 --> 00:35:10.240
So you're already kind of seeing a disconnect, how they're not really sharing about what's really going on in their lives.

854
00:35:10.660 --> 00:35:10.920
Yeah.

855
00:35:11.160 --> 00:35:13.720
They think that they're kind of protecting one another.

856
00:35:14.200 --> 00:35:19.060
In Pam's case, she's being supportive of him by not weighing him down with the day-to-day.

857
00:35:19.060 --> 00:35:24.840
And Jim feeling like he's not making her feel bad about not having new things in her life.

858
00:35:25.520 --> 00:35:29.920
Well, now we're going to move to the parking lot for our Daryl and Val storyline.

859
00:35:30.220 --> 00:35:33.680
I titled this storyline, WTF Daryl.

860
00:35:34.060 --> 00:35:35.680
Oh, we got so much mail about it.

861
00:35:35.680 --> 00:35:36.780
I don't understand.

862
00:35:36.780 --> 00:35:38.340
He was so excited.

863
00:35:38.340 --> 00:35:39.900
He liked her so much.

864
00:35:40.040 --> 00:35:44.700
And now there's a job in Philly, and he's like, I don't want to be tied down.

865
00:35:45.120 --> 00:35:45.700
Bye-bye.

866
00:35:46.100 --> 00:35:47.460
Guess who agrees with you?

867
00:35:47.940 --> 00:35:48.780
Jennifer P.

868
00:35:49.060 --> 00:35:50.200
from Spanaway, Washington.

869
00:35:50.480 --> 00:35:51.360
Thank you, Jennifer.

870
00:35:51.780 --> 00:35:54.920
Jennifer says, what's up with Daryl and the sudden 180 with Val?

871
00:35:55.140 --> 00:35:55.360
Yeah.

872
00:35:55.380 --> 00:36:00.080
After working so hard to form a relationship with Val, now he's suddenly behaving as if she's a bother?

873
00:36:00.440 --> 00:36:05.960
It was just a few episodes ago that he and Val posed hand-in-hand in a photo with Jaina.

874
00:36:05.960 --> 00:36:07.440
Jennifer, yes, Jennifer.

875
00:36:08.080 --> 00:36:10.220
They took basically a family photo.

876
00:36:10.600 --> 00:36:10.860
Yep.

877
00:36:11.240 --> 00:36:11.820
We hear you.

878
00:36:12.480 --> 00:36:12.800
Mm-hmm.

879
00:36:13.180 --> 00:36:13.400
Yeah.

880
00:36:13.840 --> 00:36:17.380
Daryl is doing that thing where he has an opportunity,

881
00:36:17.380 --> 00:36:24.600
and he's doing that thing where he thinks like his whole life is going to change or has to change because of this one new opportunity.

882
00:36:24.600 --> 00:36:28.860
But then all that happens is you're going to move to Philly and have no love in your life.

883
00:36:29.200 --> 00:36:30.300
Daryl, is that what you want?

884
00:36:30.480 --> 00:36:31.140
Think about it.

885
00:36:31.460 --> 00:36:37.860
I'm also confused by Val, too, because Val seems like she could either take him or leave him.

886
00:36:37.960 --> 00:36:41.040
I don't know that either of them are approaching this relationship in the right way.

887
00:36:41.040 --> 00:36:45.340
I feel like Val has always been a little less invested in the relationship than Daryl.

888
00:36:45.700 --> 00:36:50.080
I mean, Daryl is a step up from Brandon, but, you know.

889
00:36:50.180 --> 00:36:51.120
Maybe a sidestep.

890
00:36:51.480 --> 00:36:53.320
Slightly better than a lateral move.

891
00:36:53.980 --> 00:36:59.340
At least, you know, I don't know, Brandon seemed like a jerk to other people, maybe not to Val.

892
00:36:59.960 --> 00:37:05.860
Pam is going to go up to Meredith's desk, and she needs her supply request, but Meredith says, just stop nagging.

893
00:37:05.920 --> 00:37:07.260
Any wonder Jim left you.

894
00:37:07.420 --> 00:37:10.300
And then she starts scratching her head like really hard.

895
00:37:10.300 --> 00:37:12.180
And Pam's like, oh, no.

896
00:37:12.480 --> 00:37:13.100
Oh, no.

897
00:37:13.900 --> 00:37:15.620
Erin clocks all of this.

898
00:37:16.400 --> 00:37:16.620
Yeah.

899
00:37:16.920 --> 00:37:20.700
She starts inspecting Meredith's scalp, and guess what?

900
00:37:21.520 --> 00:37:22.160
Lice.

901
00:37:22.580 --> 00:37:27.280
Erin kind of brags she knows a lot about lice because she had it 22 times.

902
00:37:27.640 --> 00:37:27.880
Yep.

903
00:37:28.200 --> 00:37:29.300
She's an expert.

904
00:37:30.040 --> 00:37:32.420
Everyone immediately turns on Meredith.

905
00:37:32.720 --> 00:37:35.800
Angela accuses her of not signing the pledge to shower.

906
00:37:36.220 --> 00:37:38.220
Dwight is like, lock the doors.

907
00:37:38.220 --> 00:37:39.980
We're going to be under full quarantine.

908
00:37:40.300 --> 00:37:41.980
And Pam's like, relax, guys.

909
00:37:42.040 --> 00:37:42.980
It's just lice.

910
00:37:43.080 --> 00:37:43.720
I mean, maybe.

911
00:37:45.220 --> 00:37:47.060
Dwight says he had lice once.

912
00:37:47.160 --> 00:37:51.020
It was the first day of school, and he was teased for 15 years after that.

913
00:37:51.100 --> 00:37:52.060
No one would play with him.

914
00:37:52.240 --> 00:37:57.520
They called him a freak, four-eyes, sci-fi nerd, and girl puncher, all because he had lice when he was seven.

915
00:37:58.660 --> 00:37:59.460
Oh, Dwight.

916
00:37:59.460 --> 00:38:00.080
I know.

917
00:38:00.320 --> 00:38:01.240
But guess what?

918
00:38:01.340 --> 00:38:02.660
Dwight does not have lice.

919
00:38:03.080 --> 00:38:03.980
Erin inspects him.

920
00:38:04.100 --> 00:38:05.020
He is lice-free.

921
00:38:05.460 --> 00:38:08.620
And so he starts spraying everybody with a disinfectant.

922
00:38:08.740 --> 00:38:10.920
And we had a fan question from Jessica N.

923
00:38:10.980 --> 00:38:14.920
in Rochester, New York, who wanted to know, what is he spraying?

924
00:38:15.460 --> 00:38:17.540
It has to be water vapor, right?

925
00:38:18.280 --> 00:38:19.320
Yes, Jessica.

926
00:38:19.320 --> 00:38:22.880
It is an Evian water spray, like a mister.

927
00:38:22.880 --> 00:38:25.420
And we just put a different label on the can.

928
00:38:26.220 --> 00:38:27.920
Erin is now inspecting everyone.

929
00:38:28.620 --> 00:38:34.760
As she starts going through Angela's scalp, Angela reminds Meredith that this is an office, not one of her beanbag orgies.

930
00:38:35.280 --> 00:38:37.040
What is a beanbag orgy?

931
00:38:37.600 --> 00:38:40.020
Is it just an orgy on a bunch of beanbags?

932
00:38:40.360 --> 00:38:42.020
Like on a pile of beanbags?

933
00:38:42.260 --> 00:38:42.660
Oh.

934
00:38:43.400 --> 00:38:43.800
Right?

935
00:38:44.220 --> 00:38:44.820
Yeah, I guess.

936
00:38:44.820 --> 00:38:48.620
I guess it's just you throw some beanbags on the floor, and then there's an orgy?

937
00:38:48.760 --> 00:38:49.600
And you get to it.

938
00:38:49.620 --> 00:38:50.560
I didn't Google it.

939
00:38:50.560 --> 00:38:52.400
I did not Google it either.

940
00:38:52.580 --> 00:38:54.180
No, don't Google it.

941
00:38:54.200 --> 00:38:54.340
Don't do it, right?

942
00:38:54.480 --> 00:38:55.480
Put your phone away.

943
00:38:55.620 --> 00:38:56.160
Don't do it.

944
00:38:56.240 --> 00:38:56.760
Don't do it.

945
00:38:56.880 --> 00:38:57.060
Okay.

946
00:38:57.880 --> 00:38:59.780
Pam starts to come to Meredith's defense.

947
00:38:59.960 --> 00:39:02.560
She's like, you know, we're kind of blaming her prematurely.

948
00:39:02.720 --> 00:39:03.900
Oscar's not so sure.

949
00:39:04.220 --> 00:39:09.860
And then it's revealed that Angela, Stanley, Pam, and Oscar all have lice.

950
00:39:10.300 --> 00:39:11.180
All have lice.

951
00:39:11.760 --> 00:39:14.400
Dwight is going to return in a full hazmat suit.

952
00:39:14.760 --> 00:39:18.320
He says if you rent it more than four times a year, it just makes sense to buy it.

953
00:39:18.480 --> 00:39:19.600
I did look it up.

954
00:39:19.600 --> 00:39:21.400
But they're not that expensive.

955
00:39:21.840 --> 00:39:22.360
To buy?

956
00:39:22.480 --> 00:39:23.800
You can get one for like $100.

957
00:39:24.560 --> 00:39:25.360
You know what?

958
00:39:25.460 --> 00:39:29.940
This is reminding me of my recliner, which I've rented several times now.

959
00:39:30.080 --> 00:39:32.120
I keep telling you to just buy the damn thing.

960
00:39:32.240 --> 00:39:34.320
I mean, I've bought three recliners at this point.

961
00:39:34.500 --> 00:39:35.320
Just buy it.

962
00:39:35.420 --> 00:39:39.740
I know you said it doesn't really fit the aesthetic of your house, et cetera, et cetera.

963
00:39:39.840 --> 00:39:41.680
Not only, it doesn't fit in the room barely.

964
00:39:41.920 --> 00:39:44.320
We had to move the bed against the wall to fit it.

965
00:39:44.320 --> 00:39:50.040
Have you seen the ginormous dentist chair that we got Josh for his lower back?

966
00:39:50.180 --> 00:39:50.360
Yeah.

967
00:39:50.680 --> 00:39:56.740
Whenever we go to watch a show, just give yourself a minute because this is what you're going to hear.

968
00:40:02.120 --> 00:40:09.200
As he gets his legs in the right position, he has a little toggle that he can push forward or side to side.

969
00:40:09.500 --> 00:40:12.560
And then, God forbid, he's like, oh, I think I'm going to make popcorn.

970
00:40:15.080 --> 00:40:16.500
And as he gets out of the chair.

971
00:40:16.980 --> 00:40:24.400
Listen, how about when I have to go to the bathroom in the middle of the night and Lee's in the bed and I'm in the recliner and at 2 a.m., Lee has to hear.

972
00:40:25.720 --> 00:40:26.700
Oh, my gosh.

973
00:40:27.020 --> 00:40:27.960
I'd go crazy.

974
00:40:28.540 --> 00:40:29.480
I'd go crazy.

975
00:40:29.720 --> 00:40:31.340
I think I want to get an adjustable bed.

976
00:40:31.540 --> 00:40:32.160
Here's what happened.

977
00:40:32.260 --> 00:40:33.120
I broke my shoulder.

978
00:40:33.300 --> 00:40:38.780
I got so used to sleeping on my back in this one way that now I need the lift.

979
00:40:38.940 --> 00:40:39.700
You couldn't sleep.

980
00:40:39.760 --> 00:40:41.140
I couldn't sleep laying down.

981
00:40:42.140 --> 00:40:43.620
My mom, we got my mom.

982
00:40:43.860 --> 00:40:46.760
I mean, she's in her 80s, but, you know, there's no time like the present.

983
00:40:46.960 --> 00:40:47.880
You are turning 50.

984
00:40:48.420 --> 00:40:49.620
An adjustable bed.

985
00:40:49.840 --> 00:40:51.320
This is what my life has become.

986
00:40:51.620 --> 00:40:53.080
I'm leaning into it.

987
00:40:53.180 --> 00:40:54.580
I couldn't be more excited.

988
00:40:55.080 --> 00:40:55.520
Anyway.

989
00:40:55.960 --> 00:40:57.780
Dwight should have just bought the hazmat suit.

990
00:40:57.900 --> 00:40:59.020
He was right to do it.

991
00:40:59.100 --> 00:40:59.720
That's good.

992
00:41:00.080 --> 00:41:02.980
Should we talk about the folks that don't have lice, a.k.a.

993
00:41:03.040 --> 00:41:05.860
the blue group, Phyllis, Kevin, and Nellie?

994
00:41:05.960 --> 00:41:07.680
Maybe they're all the same blood type.

995
00:41:08.560 --> 00:41:09.920
Oh, maybe they are.

996
00:41:09.920 --> 00:41:10.200
Yeah.

997
00:41:10.480 --> 00:41:11.960
They're also all wearing blue.

998
00:41:13.240 --> 00:41:14.940
And Daryl doesn't have lice.

999
00:41:15.180 --> 00:41:15.980
And the warehouse.

1000
00:41:15.980 --> 00:41:16.780
They're safe.

1001
00:41:17.440 --> 00:41:20.860
Dwight is going to tell the no lice group, get out of here.

1002
00:41:21.160 --> 00:41:22.740
Go down, work in the warehouse.

1003
00:41:22.920 --> 00:41:24.200
So they're going to gather their things.

1004
00:41:24.500 --> 00:41:29.040
And when they get to the elevator, Daryl says, hey, guys, I have a few rules.

1005
00:41:29.540 --> 00:41:30.860
Don't mess with the bailer.

1006
00:41:31.060 --> 00:41:33.920
And be cool in front of me and Val because we broke up.

1007
00:41:33.920 --> 00:41:37.760
Well, Phyllis and Kevin and Nellie, they take that hard.

1008
00:41:37.940 --> 00:41:39.180
They're like, oh, my gosh.

1009
00:41:39.800 --> 00:41:40.940
That's so sad.

1010
00:41:40.940 --> 00:41:42.400
They really feel for Daryl.

1011
00:41:42.580 --> 00:41:44.420
This is going to start a whole storyline.

1012
00:41:44.720 --> 00:41:46.140
They're so nice to him.

1013
00:41:46.260 --> 00:41:46.680
I know.

1014
00:41:46.680 --> 00:41:49.000
We had a fan question from Emily B.

1015
00:41:49.220 --> 00:41:55.880
in Hillsborough, North Carolina, who said, what's up with Kevin kissing so many people on the cheek in this episode?

1016
00:41:56.060 --> 00:41:57.760
First Daryl and later Val.

1017
00:41:58.140 --> 00:42:00.520
Was that scripted or improvised?

1018
00:42:01.280 --> 00:42:06.740
Well, Emily, I went to the script and I found out something very interesting.

1019
00:42:07.060 --> 00:42:08.140
Oh, let's hear it.

1020
00:42:08.440 --> 00:42:14.780
So this scene was shorter in the shooting draft than what ended up in the episode.

1021
00:42:14.820 --> 00:42:15.780
When do we ever say that?

1022
00:42:16.160 --> 00:42:16.460
Shorter.

1023
00:42:17.160 --> 00:42:17.720
Yeah.

1024
00:42:18.100 --> 00:42:19.640
Here's what I found.

1025
00:42:19.880 --> 00:42:23.440
It ended after Daryl gave them the news about the breakup.

1026
00:42:23.440 --> 00:42:32.620
That whole second part about them trying to comfort him and Kevin giving him his chocolate bar and Nellie saying that the singer Brandy got her through.

1027
00:42:32.740 --> 00:42:35.540
None of that was in our shooting script.

1028
00:42:35.760 --> 00:42:37.500
All of this was added later.

1029
00:42:37.640 --> 00:42:43.560
There was a script rewrite page handed out on the day that we shot this.

1030
00:42:43.880 --> 00:42:47.240
And that is where all of this extra detail came out.

1031
00:42:47.560 --> 00:42:50.260
There was nothing about Kevin giving Daryl a kiss.

1032
00:42:50.260 --> 00:42:52.560
I guess that was just something they came up with.

1033
00:42:53.240 --> 00:42:58.760
However, originally, Kevin was holding a bag of potato chips and he offers Daryl the potato chips.

1034
00:42:59.540 --> 00:43:01.360
Somehow that got changed to candy bar.

1035
00:43:01.680 --> 00:43:05.000
I wonder if Brian improvised the kiss on Daryl's cheek.

1036
00:43:05.360 --> 00:43:07.160
And then maybe later to Val.

1037
00:43:07.480 --> 00:43:07.680
Yeah.

1038
00:43:07.820 --> 00:43:09.340
Because neither of those were scripted.

1039
00:43:10.000 --> 00:43:10.300
Mm-hmm.

1040
00:43:10.540 --> 00:43:13.960
Well, I thought Craig's reaction as Daryl was really funny.

1041
00:43:14.300 --> 00:43:15.860
Maybe because it was a surprise.

1042
00:43:16.080 --> 00:43:16.240
Yeah.

1043
00:43:16.900 --> 00:43:18.280
Pam now has a talking head.

1044
00:43:18.520 --> 00:43:20.660
And Jenna, you're so good in it.

1045
00:43:20.660 --> 00:43:23.180
Because you start off so defiant.

1046
00:43:23.380 --> 00:43:23.860
You're like, you know what?

1047
00:43:23.960 --> 00:43:25.380
Maybe Meredith did bring lights.

1048
00:43:25.380 --> 00:43:27.180
And they're different from the ones that Cece got.

1049
00:43:27.340 --> 00:43:28.940
And don't jump to conclusions.

1050
00:43:28.940 --> 00:43:30.180
That's how worse gets started.

1051
00:43:30.380 --> 00:43:36.420
And then when Pam just gives in and is like, fine, I'll tell her.

1052
00:43:36.640 --> 00:43:37.360
I'll confess.

1053
00:43:38.080 --> 00:43:40.360
I thought it was such a good talking head.

1054
00:43:40.540 --> 00:43:41.440
I loved your performance.

1055
00:43:41.960 --> 00:43:42.820
Thank you so much.

1056
00:43:42.960 --> 00:43:50.020
When I watched it, it reminded me of Jeremy being confronted by Laura in Love is Blind, season six.

1057
00:43:50.240 --> 00:43:51.600
I don't watch Love is Blind.

1058
00:43:51.600 --> 00:43:53.920
And he stayed out at the bar till 5 a.m.

1059
00:43:54.380 --> 00:43:55.160
Oh, my God.

1060
00:43:55.420 --> 00:43:56.400
This is so specific.

1061
00:43:56.840 --> 00:43:59.260
Anyone who watched that season will know what I'm talking about.

1062
00:43:59.400 --> 00:44:04.400
But when I saw Jeremy do that moment with Laura, it also reminded me of Michael Scott

1063
00:44:04.400 --> 00:44:08.180
and how defensive he is about burning his foot on the George Foreman grill.

1064
00:44:08.940 --> 00:44:11.640
This guy, Jeremy, he just didn't come home.

1065
00:44:11.980 --> 00:44:14.000
And he's sitting in the living room.

1066
00:44:14.140 --> 00:44:14.840
It's like 6 a.m.

1067
00:44:14.840 --> 00:44:16.880
He's got glasses on, sunglasses on.

1068
00:44:17.100 --> 00:44:18.560
And his fiancée comes in.

1069
00:44:18.640 --> 00:44:20.720
She's like, are we leaving the glasses on all day?

1070
00:44:21.620 --> 00:44:23.260
And he just takes him off.

1071
00:44:23.340 --> 00:44:24.100
She's super calm.

1072
00:44:24.540 --> 00:44:26.380
And he's like, what, do you want to talk about it?

1073
00:44:26.860 --> 00:44:28.060
She's like, I think we should.

1074
00:44:28.220 --> 00:44:30.240
Yeah, you didn't come home last night.

1075
00:44:30.980 --> 00:44:32.940
And he's like, what do you want me to say?

1076
00:44:33.100 --> 00:44:34.600
I went out with my friends.

1077
00:44:34.680 --> 00:44:37.960
And then, okay, Sarah Ann showed up.

1078
00:44:37.980 --> 00:44:39.500
What am I supposed to do?

1079
00:44:39.700 --> 00:44:40.980
I had to talk to her.

1080
00:44:41.160 --> 00:44:42.420
We had to get closure.

1081
00:44:42.420 --> 00:44:45.420
And she's like, yeah, the bar closes at 2 a.m.

1082
00:44:45.620 --> 00:44:47.080
Where were you from 2 to 5?

1083
00:44:47.180 --> 00:44:48.940
He's like, we were in a car.

1084
00:44:48.940 --> 00:44:50.540
We were talking, okay?

1085
00:44:50.540 --> 00:44:52.280
I sent you my location.

1086
00:44:52.560 --> 00:44:55.760
But it's just like super defensive.

1087
00:44:55.960 --> 00:44:58.500
Like, dude, it's you.

1088
00:44:58.660 --> 00:44:59.720
It's on you, buddy.

1089
00:44:59.880 --> 00:45:01.340
It is on you, bud.

1090
00:45:01.800 --> 00:45:06.860
Any question that your fiancée has about your whereabouts last night are super valid.

1091
00:45:07.200 --> 00:45:07.460
Yeah.

1092
00:45:08.080 --> 00:45:10.060
Does he ever say, okay, fine?

1093
00:45:10.640 --> 00:45:11.160
No.

1094
00:45:11.420 --> 00:45:11.840
Oh, my gosh.

1095
00:45:11.840 --> 00:45:15.780
And she just sort of remains sort of like, kind of like, oh, fine.

1096
00:45:15.960 --> 00:45:17.140
I'll tell you again.

1097
00:45:17.400 --> 00:45:18.660
We were in the car.

1098
00:45:18.940 --> 00:45:20.140
We were talking.

1099
00:45:20.320 --> 00:45:21.600
It's very Michael Scott.

1100
00:45:21.600 --> 00:45:23.900
Like, I like the smell of bacon, okay?

1101
00:45:24.340 --> 00:45:25.120
Sue me.

1102
00:45:25.360 --> 00:45:29.200
And then she's like, how did Sarah Ann get home?

1103
00:45:29.280 --> 00:45:32.040
And he's like, yes, I drove her home.

1104
00:45:35.160 --> 00:45:38.220
Sarah's like, wait, it's getting worse.

1105
00:45:38.220 --> 00:45:41.660
But it's like, why do you have bed head?

1106
00:45:42.140 --> 00:45:42.540
Duh.

1107
00:45:42.680 --> 00:45:43.760
I was tired.

1108
00:45:44.500 --> 00:45:46.400
She said I could lay on her bed.

1109
00:45:46.600 --> 00:45:48.220
What, you want me to drive home tired?

1110
00:45:48.400 --> 00:45:49.820
You want me to draw you a map?

1111
00:45:49.820 --> 00:45:51.500
It was so funny.

1112
00:45:51.740 --> 00:45:51.820
Oh, my gosh.

1113
00:45:52.020 --> 00:45:52.960
I'm so sorry.

1114
00:45:53.300 --> 00:45:55.600
Jeremy, I'm sure you're a nice person.

1115
00:45:55.920 --> 00:46:01.040
And you became fodder for the internet with this scene.

1116
00:46:01.320 --> 00:46:02.940
So many people have recreated it.

1117
00:46:03.160 --> 00:46:05.060
I don't know anything you're talking about.

1118
00:46:05.140 --> 00:46:05.460
I know.

1119
00:46:05.720 --> 00:46:05.770
Like, nothing.

1120
00:46:05.880 --> 00:46:06.240
I'm sorry.

1121
00:46:06.240 --> 00:46:08.440
I'm not going to have to look it up because I'm now fascinated.

1122
00:46:08.480 --> 00:46:09.920
I'm tangent lady today.

1123
00:46:10.140 --> 00:46:10.400
Okay.

1124
00:46:10.400 --> 00:46:11.200
Apologize.

1125
00:46:11.740 --> 00:46:13.320
Listen, where are we?

1126
00:46:13.500 --> 00:46:14.300
We're in a limo.

1127
00:46:14.780 --> 00:46:14.900
Okay.

1128
00:46:15.200 --> 00:46:18.300
Jim is downing what I think are mimosas.

1129
00:46:18.580 --> 00:46:20.900
Is this orange juice fresh squeezed, he asks.

1130
00:46:21.320 --> 00:46:22.280
He's tickled.

1131
00:46:22.400 --> 00:46:24.160
He asks if he can take some snacks.

1132
00:46:24.680 --> 00:46:28.720
And the limo driver drops him off on the sidewalk.

1133
00:46:28.920 --> 00:46:33.240
And he's like, wait, is this, where am I?

1134
00:46:33.400 --> 00:46:36.780
And he says, this is Dr. J's private court.

1135
00:46:36.940 --> 00:46:38.040
You'll be meeting him here.

1136
00:46:38.040 --> 00:46:40.660
Jim is like, you've got to be kidding me.

1137
00:46:40.880 --> 00:46:41.100
Yeah.

1138
00:46:41.820 --> 00:46:46.500
Well, I have a fun story about the limo driver in this scene.

1139
00:46:46.720 --> 00:46:47.960
I know this story.

1140
00:46:48.200 --> 00:46:50.280
You called me after and I was like, what?

1141
00:46:50.640 --> 00:46:51.120
I know.

1142
00:46:51.340 --> 00:46:53.200
This is, talk about random coincidence.

1143
00:46:53.580 --> 00:46:57.180
So earlier this year, I was filming a project out of town.

1144
00:46:57.320 --> 00:46:59.520
I can't share about it yet, but I can't wait to tell you guys.

1145
00:46:59.640 --> 00:47:00.280
It was super fun.

1146
00:47:00.420 --> 00:47:04.900
So I'm filming out of town and the production company arranged for a car to pick me up from

1147
00:47:04.900 --> 00:47:05.380
the airport.

1148
00:47:05.600 --> 00:47:05.840
Yep.

1149
00:47:05.840 --> 00:47:09.840
I get in the car and the driver was really nice.

1150
00:47:10.180 --> 00:47:14.000
And we get to talking and he was like, gosh, you look familiar.

1151
00:47:14.320 --> 00:47:16.180
And I was like, I know you look familiar too.

1152
00:47:16.460 --> 00:47:17.320
And we're just like, huh.

1153
00:47:18.160 --> 00:47:21.780
And then we sort of ride in silence and he's like, wait, were you on The Office?

1154
00:47:22.040 --> 00:47:23.060
And I said, yeah, I was.

1155
00:47:23.160 --> 00:47:24.660
I played, you know, Angela in accounting.

1156
00:47:25.560 --> 00:47:28.040
And he said, I was on The Office too.

1157
00:47:28.260 --> 00:47:29.460
And I said, what?

1158
00:47:29.780 --> 00:47:30.720
This is so crazy.

1159
00:47:30.720 --> 00:47:31.200
Yeah.

1160
00:47:31.420 --> 00:47:33.120
He said, okay, it's season nine.

1161
00:47:33.280 --> 00:47:35.860
And I was like, wait, I do a podcast and we just started season nine.

1162
00:47:36.160 --> 00:47:41.300
He goes, okay, remember when Jim gets picked up in a limo to go meet Dr. J?

1163
00:47:41.560 --> 00:47:43.780
And I was like, oh my God, that was you?

1164
00:47:43.880 --> 00:47:44.840
And he said, yes.

1165
00:47:45.460 --> 00:47:47.000
His name is Jeff Hatch.

1166
00:47:47.200 --> 00:47:48.980
He is the loveliest person.

1167
00:47:49.460 --> 00:47:53.000
And I was like, Jeff, can I interview you for my podcast?

1168
00:47:54.060 --> 00:47:56.240
We're driving down the 405 freeway.

1169
00:47:56.420 --> 00:47:56.960
He's like, sure.

1170
00:47:57.120 --> 00:47:58.080
I'm in the back seat.

1171
00:47:58.200 --> 00:48:01.280
So I'm kind of leaning forward and he's kind of facing forward.

1172
00:48:01.460 --> 00:48:05.280
The sound quality is probably not the best, but he was so lovely.

1173
00:48:05.280 --> 00:48:09.940
And this was such a fun reconnection moment, a little mini office reunion.

1174
00:48:09.940 --> 00:48:11.140
I want you to hear it.

1175
00:48:11.240 --> 00:48:12.580
I love this.

1176
00:48:13.800 --> 00:48:16.180
Hello, office ladies, listeners.

1177
00:48:16.180 --> 00:48:18.400
I am in the car with Jeff Hatch.

1178
00:48:18.400 --> 00:48:18.880
Hi.

1179
00:48:19.160 --> 00:48:21.840
He played the limo driver in which episode?

1180
00:48:22.060 --> 00:48:23.560
It was the episode Lice.

1181
00:48:23.760 --> 00:48:27.640
And John Krasinski's character was out of the office the day they had lice.

1182
00:48:27.900 --> 00:48:32.840
Because he was meeting Dr. J.

1183
00:48:33.140 --> 00:48:33.860
Oh, yeah.

1184
00:48:34.160 --> 00:48:37.320
The basketball player in Portland, Oregon.

1185
00:48:37.320 --> 00:48:45.260
And I was briefly on screen as the limo driver that picked him up and took him to Dr. J's office.

1186
00:48:45.640 --> 00:48:48.080
And how did you get your job on the office?

1187
00:48:48.400 --> 00:48:59.200
Um, I had a class B commercial license and I could drive stretch limos because that was my job at the time and still is my job to this day.

1188
00:48:59.200 --> 00:49:09.000
Uh, and I, uh, I delivered the lines halfway convincingly and I happened to have a SAG card.

1189
00:49:09.200 --> 00:49:11.220
So that was, that was the whole requirement.

1190
00:49:11.480 --> 00:49:12.080
There you go.

1191
00:49:12.160 --> 00:49:13.500
And you had three lines?

1192
00:49:13.660 --> 00:49:14.460
Had three lines.

1193
00:49:14.640 --> 00:49:15.420
One of them got cut.

1194
00:49:15.420 --> 00:49:20.460
So you, you get to enjoy me delivering two lines to John Krasinski.

1195
00:49:20.720 --> 00:49:23.380
And we just met at the airport.

1196
00:49:23.620 --> 00:49:26.880
We just met at the airport, uh, doing my job as a limo driver.

1197
00:49:27.220 --> 00:49:29.840
The, the actual limo driver job.

1198
00:49:30.000 --> 00:49:31.680
Not the, not the television version.

1199
00:49:32.480 --> 00:49:33.040
Awesome.

1200
00:49:33.260 --> 00:49:33.440
Awesome.

1201
00:49:33.660 --> 00:49:35.500
Thank you so much for being on Office Ladies.

1202
00:49:35.880 --> 00:49:36.580
My pleasure.

1203
00:49:38.840 --> 00:49:41.000
I love that so much.

1204
00:49:41.320 --> 00:49:42.640
How random is that?

1205
00:49:43.040 --> 00:49:43.500
I mean.

1206
00:49:43.760 --> 00:49:44.480
So crazy.

1207
00:49:44.880 --> 00:49:47.180
And you guys, we weren't in a limo just so you know.

1208
00:49:47.300 --> 00:49:48.720
It was just one of those big SUvs.

1209
00:49:48.820 --> 00:49:49.260
Oh, yeah, yeah.

1210
00:49:49.260 --> 00:49:49.540
Yeah, yeah.

1211
00:49:49.540 --> 00:49:54.460
But he was so lovely and I'm going to give a shout out to him in stories.

1212
00:49:55.000 --> 00:49:57.800
Jeff, thanks for talking to me about your time on the office.

1213
00:49:58.160 --> 00:49:59.000
That is so cool.

1214
00:49:59.300 --> 00:50:05.780
Well, I know that whenever we had to have someone who was actually driving a car, you had to have that special.

1215
00:50:06.040 --> 00:50:06.420
A professional driver.

1216
00:50:06.600 --> 00:50:09.420
Yeah, a special license and also be an actor.

1217
00:50:09.640 --> 00:50:12.360
And so we would cast people with those criteria.

1218
00:50:12.660 --> 00:50:13.480
And he did great.

1219
00:50:13.880 --> 00:50:14.400
I know.

1220
00:50:14.740 --> 00:50:15.680
I thought it was awesome.

1221
00:50:15.900 --> 00:50:16.520
Very believable.

1222
00:50:16.720 --> 00:50:17.420
Very believable.

1223
00:50:17.620 --> 00:50:18.260
So natural.

1224
00:50:18.260 --> 00:50:20.280
Natural and just a lovely person.

1225
00:50:20.820 --> 00:50:20.980
Aw.

1226
00:50:21.240 --> 00:50:23.200
Well, on that note, why don't we take a break?

1227
00:50:23.560 --> 00:50:27.300
I've been slowly eating this cake all through this last segment.

1228
00:50:27.300 --> 00:50:31.320
I know it's been distracting you, Angela, but you can't give me cake and then make me wait to eat it.

1229
00:50:31.380 --> 00:50:32.820
I'm a lady who likes cake.

1230
00:50:32.920 --> 00:50:33.300
I know.

1231
00:50:33.340 --> 00:50:37.760
But I was also watching you eat it and watching you try not to make noise while you eat it.

1232
00:50:37.900 --> 00:50:38.100
I know.

1233
00:50:38.380 --> 00:50:40.860
So that, like, imagine someone taking a bite.

1234
00:50:40.920 --> 00:50:41.020
Of course, it's more distracting.

1235
00:50:41.380 --> 00:50:44.300
But they're trying not to let their lips fully touch the fork.

1236
00:50:44.480 --> 00:50:45.760
So it's like, oh, boom.

1237
00:50:45.840 --> 00:50:46.320
So sorry.

1238
00:50:48.360 --> 00:50:54.440
Okay, we'll be right back because Pam is going to go into the kitchen to find Meredith shaving her head.

1239
00:50:54.800 --> 00:51:07.530
Well, here we are.

1240
00:51:07.810 --> 00:51:08.490
We're in the kitchen.

1241
00:51:09.090 --> 00:51:11.110
Meredith is going to start to shave her head.

1242
00:51:11.310 --> 00:51:15.930
She also is heating up some wax for down south.

1243
00:51:16.090 --> 00:51:16.690
That's right.

1244
00:51:16.870 --> 00:51:18.430
Just in case the critters migrated.

1245
00:51:18.430 --> 00:51:28.050
Yeah, Pam enters and she's going to confess, but she doesn't have time because Meredith has shaved the center of her head already.

1246
00:51:28.350 --> 00:51:30.450
I mean, could you imagine?

1247
00:51:30.770 --> 00:51:31.090
No.

1248
00:51:31.350 --> 00:51:32.170
I can't.

1249
00:51:32.290 --> 00:51:32.870
Oh, my goodness.

1250
00:51:33.270 --> 00:51:40.910
We had a fan question from Rosie Kay from Valley, Nebraska, who said, I need to know all about the scene where Meredith is shaving her head.

1251
00:51:40.910 --> 00:51:44.430
Obviously, she didn't really shave her head, but it looks so real.

1252
00:51:44.730 --> 00:51:46.930
How did they go about making this look so real?

1253
00:51:47.330 --> 00:51:49.410
Is she wearing a cap with a wig?

1254
00:51:49.410 --> 00:51:50.410
I must know.

1255
00:51:50.410 --> 00:51:56.590
Oh, well, Kate sent us in an audio clip sharing all about this, and you got to hear it.

1256
00:51:57.510 --> 00:52:03.570
How that all worked, all the scenes worked, especially the one where I'm specifically shaving my head, like where you actually see it.

1257
00:52:04.310 --> 00:52:09.770
Yeah, it took like three and a half hours to get into the bald cap with a partial wig for that scene.

1258
00:52:09.770 --> 00:52:11.870
So I look like Benjamin Franklin.

1259
00:52:12.210 --> 00:52:15.670
And then they had me put hair in my hand.

1260
00:52:15.670 --> 00:52:20.590
Like I actually had my hand on top of my head holding the extra hair so you couldn't tell.

1261
00:52:20.850 --> 00:52:21.850
It was a pretty quick shot.

1262
00:52:22.030 --> 00:52:29.430
And then I had the razor in my right hand, hair on top of my head with my left hand, and then I just rolled it over and just like let the hair drop.

1263
00:52:29.630 --> 00:52:32.390
