1532
01:02:24.930 --> 01:02:27.550
Like, you know, because they are very sheer.

1533
01:02:27.910 --> 01:02:29.990
What's going to happen when someone slides?

1534
01:02:30.250 --> 01:02:32.270
Are they durable but sheer?

1535
01:02:32.270 --> 01:02:32.930
We don't know.

1536
01:02:33.050 --> 01:02:33.650
We don't know yet.

1537
01:02:33.650 --> 01:02:34.870
They've got to be durable.

1538
01:02:35.150 --> 01:02:36.090
None of them want to slide.

1539
01:02:36.350 --> 01:02:37.830
None of the white pants teaMs.

1540
01:02:38.030 --> 01:02:39.430
Nobody wants to slide.

1541
01:02:40.250 --> 01:02:42.150
It's going to be – what's going to happen?

1542
01:02:42.630 --> 01:02:43.470
Oh, wait.

1543
01:02:43.630 --> 01:02:44.650
Jordan has an update.

1544
01:02:45.310 --> 01:02:45.730
Yeah.

1545
01:02:45.890 --> 01:02:47.990
So this is from sportsillustrated.com.

1546
01:02:48.090 --> 01:02:54.070
And the MLB said in a statement, the uniform pants have the same material and thickness

1547
01:02:54.070 --> 01:02:56.230
as the uniform pants used last season.

1548
01:02:56.410 --> 01:02:59.910
There were changes to the fabric of the jersey, not the pants.

1549
01:03:00.230 --> 01:03:00.730
No.

1550
01:03:01.250 --> 01:03:03.110
There's no way.

1551
01:03:03.650 --> 01:03:06.270
The pants did not look like this last year.

1552
01:03:07.310 --> 01:03:08.810
That cannot be possible.

1553
01:03:09.070 --> 01:03:10.590
This is a cover-up story.

1554
01:03:10.850 --> 01:03:12.030
Mom detectives!

1555
01:03:12.310 --> 01:03:12.550
We're honeSt.

1556
01:03:12.550 --> 01:03:14.110
The taste of the see-through pants.

1557
01:03:14.110 --> 01:03:16.110
I guess we have to go to Dodger Stadium now.

1558
01:03:16.230 --> 01:03:16.670
We do.

1559
01:03:17.170 --> 01:03:18.110
Oh, my gosh.

1560
01:03:18.110 --> 01:03:19.650
I don't even know where we are.

1561
01:03:19.770 --> 01:03:21.930
I'm so sorry for that crazy tangent.

1562
01:03:22.430 --> 01:03:25.390
Oh, because we were talking about Dr. J's shoes.

1563
01:03:25.410 --> 01:03:26.090
Dr. J and his shoes.

1564
01:03:26.690 --> 01:03:28.110
I'm Tangent Lady today.

1565
01:03:28.330 --> 01:03:30.310
Well, I'll take us back to the conference room.

1566
01:03:30.410 --> 01:03:30.810
Okay.

1567
01:03:31.530 --> 01:03:33.670
Mayonnaise is being distributed, y'all.

1568
01:03:33.830 --> 01:03:34.210
Mm-hmm.

1569
01:03:34.730 --> 01:03:35.090
Okay.

1570
01:03:35.470 --> 01:03:36.890
They're going to split up into pairs.

1571
01:03:36.890 --> 01:03:37.350
Yeah.

1572
01:03:37.590 --> 01:03:43.630
And while Dwight is sort of talking to everyone about this, he cuts his own hazmat suit with

1573
01:03:43.630 --> 01:03:44.170
the scissors.

1574
01:03:44.630 --> 01:03:45.790
He freaks out.

1575
01:03:45.910 --> 01:03:46.810
He runs out of the room.

1576
01:03:47.270 --> 01:03:47.530
Yes.

1577
01:03:47.890 --> 01:03:49.730
Fan question from Claudia S.

1578
01:03:49.830 --> 01:03:50.570
in Sydney, Australia.

1579
01:03:50.890 --> 01:03:53.470
I never heard of killing lice with mayonnaise.

1580
01:03:53.910 --> 01:03:55.210
Does that actually work?

1581
01:03:56.070 --> 01:03:58.210
Well, fan question from Ava F.

1582
01:03:58.390 --> 01:04:03.110
in Hadesburg, Mississippi says, yes, you can put mayo on

1583
01:04:03.110 --> 01:04:07.650
your hair and it will suffocate the lice, but you need to leave it on for six to eight

1584
01:04:07.650 --> 01:04:09.630
hours, not just four hours.

1585
01:04:09.810 --> 01:04:12.450
And then seven to eight days later, you have to do it again.

1586
01:04:13.050 --> 01:04:14.550
You can also use olive oil.

1587
01:04:14.770 --> 01:04:17.170
I feel like this is all stuff my grandmother knew.

1588
01:04:17.390 --> 01:04:21.150
Like, we would get a bug bite and she'd be like, go get clear nail polish.

1589
01:04:21.570 --> 01:04:22.410
I'm going to put a little...

1590
01:04:22.410 --> 01:04:22.710
That works.

1591
01:04:22.930 --> 01:04:23.250
Yes.

1592
01:04:23.430 --> 01:04:24.950
It suffocates the little bug.

1593
01:04:25.210 --> 01:04:26.810
Yeah, you're right.

1594
01:04:27.070 --> 01:04:28.590
I forgot about that trick.

1595
01:04:28.890 --> 01:04:29.130
Yeah.

1596
01:04:29.550 --> 01:04:31.990
So I guess, yes, you can use mayo.

1597
01:04:32.110 --> 01:04:34.990
I think I would just use like a lice shampoo though.

1598
01:04:35.270 --> 01:04:36.370
Why are you whispering it?

1599
01:04:36.430 --> 01:04:37.270
Are you just telling me?

1600
01:04:37.390 --> 01:04:38.550
Are you whispering to everybody?

1601
01:04:38.910 --> 01:04:43.890
I mean, I guess everyone's going to know, but I would just go with the, I don't think

1602
01:04:43.890 --> 01:04:44.710
I would do mayo.

1603
01:04:45.530 --> 01:04:46.230
You know what?

1604
01:04:46.350 --> 01:04:47.730
Sometimes you got to work with what you got.

1605
01:04:48.050 --> 01:04:48.890
Well, that's true.

1606
01:04:48.970 --> 01:04:51.750
If you got mayo and it's bad, use the mayo, I guess.

1607
01:04:51.750 --> 01:04:53.270
If I was out in the woods.

1608
01:04:53.550 --> 01:04:53.890
Yeah.

1609
01:04:53.890 --> 01:04:56.330
I would just use mayo or olive oil.

1610
01:04:56.610 --> 01:04:58.570
Here is who all got paired up together.

1611
01:04:58.790 --> 01:04:59.630
Angela and Oscar.

1612
01:05:00.350 --> 01:05:01.470
Aaron and Pete.

1613
01:05:01.910 --> 01:05:02.710
Creed and Pam.

1614
01:05:02.970 --> 01:05:03.830
Creed goes great.

1615
01:05:03.950 --> 01:05:05.190
I got stuck with the weirdo.

1616
01:05:05.350 --> 01:05:05.630
Mm-hmm.

1617
01:05:06.290 --> 01:05:09.250
Angela's going to really slap that mayonnaise onto Oscar's head.

1618
01:05:09.530 --> 01:05:12.810
Angela says you don't want bugs because who knows where those bugs will end up.

1619
01:05:12.990 --> 01:05:17.770
She's clearly still very angry at Oscar and is going to really enjoy putting this mayonnaise

1620
01:05:17.770 --> 01:05:18.450
on his head.

1621
01:05:18.590 --> 01:05:25.230
We have a very cute mayo application montage with Pete and Aaron.

1622
01:05:25.630 --> 01:05:26.470
Oh, yeah.

1623
01:05:26.910 --> 01:05:30.490
I went to the script and here is what it said.

1624
01:05:30.730 --> 01:05:37.150
Quote, Aaron and Pete, both with their heads lathered in mayo, ad-lib flirting.

1625
01:05:37.530 --> 01:05:39.050
Some suggested areas.

1626
01:05:39.270 --> 01:05:41.750
Aaron pushes all his hair into a mohawk.

1627
01:05:42.210 --> 01:05:44.390
Aaron arranges her hair in a Martha Washington.

1628
01:05:44.390 --> 01:05:46.070
Have fun on set.

1629
01:05:46.570 --> 01:05:47.490
Budget 30 minutes.

1630
01:05:48.570 --> 01:05:49.630
That's very funny.

1631
01:05:49.790 --> 01:05:51.410
I've never seen that before in a script.

1632
01:05:51.690 --> 01:05:52.210
I know.

1633
01:05:52.330 --> 01:05:53.090
That's very cute.

1634
01:05:53.430 --> 01:05:55.450
Well, I thought that scene was adorable.

1635
01:05:55.450 --> 01:06:01.110
And I feel like when Ellie, as Aaron says, Eiffel Tower, that that was Jake's real laugh.

1636
01:06:01.110 --> 01:06:01.950
Me too.

1637
01:06:02.210 --> 01:06:02.870
Me too.

1638
01:06:03.170 --> 01:06:04.850
We got a fan mail flurry.

1639
01:06:05.030 --> 01:06:10.310
People wanted to know if it was real mayonnaise and if not, what was used and did it smell

1640
01:06:10.310 --> 01:06:13.030
and how long did it take to wash out of our hair afterwards?

1641
01:06:13.550 --> 01:06:20.670
My memory is that we used a thick hair conditioner and that my hair was very, very, very conditioned

1642
01:06:20.670 --> 01:06:21.390
and soft.

1643
01:06:21.650 --> 01:06:23.130
Yes, that's exactly what it was.

1644
01:06:23.250 --> 01:06:24.390
That's my memory as well.

1645
01:06:24.610 --> 01:06:27.470
And it looked like mayonnaise, but actually smelled pretty good.

1646
01:06:27.470 --> 01:06:28.590
It was just a hair conditioner.

1647
01:06:29.130 --> 01:06:32.250
I took my camera to set that day and I have some great pictures.

1648
01:06:32.410 --> 01:06:37.510
I put them in our book, The Office BFFs, but the only photo I have of myself and Jake

1649
01:06:37.510 --> 01:06:42.510
Lacey, just the two of us from his whole time on the show, is the two of us with this

1650
01:06:42.510 --> 01:06:44.030
mayonnaise on our heads.

1651
01:06:45.090 --> 01:06:46.010
That's very funny.

1652
01:06:46.350 --> 01:06:48.730
You know, we also had a fan question from Melissa S.

1653
01:06:48.890 --> 01:06:50.810
in Statesville, North Carolina, who

1654
01:06:50.810 --> 01:06:53.950
said, how long on average did you have to keep that on your hair?

1655
01:06:54.570 --> 01:06:57.950
I know sometimes one or two scenes can take multiple hours.

1656
01:06:58.910 --> 01:07:06.010
Well, I remembered that we grouped these mayonnaise scenes together and Steve Burgess confirmed

1657
01:07:06.010 --> 01:07:06.310
that.

1658
01:07:06.590 --> 01:07:11.510
He said we did a full day and a half day of mayo hair.

1659
01:07:11.850 --> 01:07:12.010
Yeah.

1660
01:07:12.310 --> 01:07:18.430
I also remember my head being cold because it was like we had a hair mask on.

1661
01:07:18.730 --> 01:07:19.130
Yeah.

1662
01:07:19.450 --> 01:07:20.750
It was very, like, damp.

1663
01:07:20.750 --> 01:07:24.890
And it sort of took the temperature of the room and our set was really cold.

1664
01:07:25.050 --> 01:07:25.350
Mm-hmm.

1665
01:07:25.850 --> 01:07:32.490
Meredith applies mayo to Stanley and Pam does the mayo on Creed's scalp, but then Creed doesn't

1666
01:07:32.490 --> 01:07:33.470
want to do Pam's.

1667
01:07:33.730 --> 01:07:35.930
So now Pam is left trying to do her own.

1668
01:07:36.130 --> 01:07:36.830
I know.

1669
01:07:37.390 --> 01:07:43.010
Well, in this sort of really messy process of her putting mayo on her own hair, her phone

1670
01:07:43.010 --> 01:07:47.070
rings and she can't answer it because she's got the mayonnaise all over her fingers.

1671
01:07:47.070 --> 01:07:50.690
So with her elbow, she kind of hits the speakerphone button and it's her mom.

1672
01:07:51.430 --> 01:07:57.170
And her mom announces to the whole bullpen that CeCe's school says she still has lice

1673
01:07:57.170 --> 01:07:58.510
and Pam might have it too.

1674
01:07:58.970 --> 01:08:02.210
Pam rushes to hang up the phone, but that's it.

1675
01:08:02.450 --> 01:08:04.610
Everyone has locked in on this.

1676
01:08:04.770 --> 01:08:06.170
They can't believe it.

1677
01:08:06.470 --> 01:08:10.010
And Jenna, I remember this moment at the table read when we read the script.

1678
01:08:10.010 --> 01:08:14.810
The whole room erupted into laughter and I wanted to read how it was in the script.

1679
01:08:15.570 --> 01:08:18.590
Pam finally manages to hang up, but it's too late.

1680
01:08:18.770 --> 01:08:25.950
Everybody stares at her, completely aware that Pam is actually patient zero, not Meredith.

1681
01:08:26.370 --> 01:08:29.590
Angela says, oh my God.

1682
01:08:30.050 --> 01:08:34.470
Off Pam's horror, Meredith says, shave her head.

1683
01:08:34.690 --> 01:08:36.610
Shave her head!

1684
01:08:37.870 --> 01:08:40.330
And Kate crushed it.

1685
01:08:41.010 --> 01:08:42.490
It's so funny.

1686
01:08:42.710 --> 01:08:43.550
I remember that.

1687
01:08:43.730 --> 01:08:46.690
This was a really, really fun scene to shoot.

1688
01:08:47.030 --> 01:08:50.450
I loved all the mayo falling off my fingers.

1689
01:08:50.650 --> 01:08:51.070
Klutzy.

1690
01:08:51.350 --> 01:08:52.350
Klutzy acting.

1691
01:08:52.470 --> 01:08:52.850
I know.

1692
01:08:53.030 --> 01:08:53.210
Again.

1693
01:08:53.470 --> 01:08:55.030
Save it for mom detectives, lady.

1694
01:08:55.810 --> 01:08:57.890
Well, everyone starts to yell at Pam.

1695
01:08:58.030 --> 01:08:58.610
She's apologizing.

1696
01:08:59.210 --> 01:09:01.850
She said it's been so hectic with Jim being gone.

1697
01:09:01.850 --> 01:09:04.610
And she really does apologize to Meredith.

1698
01:09:04.910 --> 01:09:08.430
And that's when Angela's like, a lot of good that does now.

1699
01:09:08.570 --> 01:09:09.470
She's a monster.

1700
01:09:09.750 --> 01:09:10.090
Yes.

1701
01:09:10.730 --> 01:09:14.490
Then I just loved this next Meredith talking head.

1702
01:09:14.590 --> 01:09:15.390
I loved it.

1703
01:09:15.690 --> 01:09:18.830
Kate was so phenomenal in it, I thought we should hear it.

1704
01:09:19.450 --> 01:09:22.390
Who's the one that didn't bring Lice into the office?

1705
01:09:22.750 --> 01:09:23.310
Meredith.

1706
01:09:23.950 --> 01:09:27.770
Sure, I gave everybody pink eye once and my ex keyed a few of their cars.

1707
01:09:27.770 --> 01:09:32.730
And yeah, I BM'd in the shredder on New Year's, but I didn't bring the Lice in.

1708
01:09:33.110 --> 01:09:35.350
That was all Pam.

1709
01:09:36.130 --> 01:09:37.390
I love it so much.

1710
01:09:37.430 --> 01:09:37.990
Perfection.

1711
01:09:38.150 --> 01:09:38.810
So good.

1712
01:09:38.950 --> 01:09:40.470
We learned so much information.

1713
01:09:40.670 --> 01:09:41.230
Yes.

1714
01:09:41.610 --> 01:09:44.790
Apparently, Meredith did give everyone pink eye once.

1715
01:09:45.350 --> 01:09:47.190
Everybody's cars got keyed.

1716
01:09:47.750 --> 01:09:49.990
And she took a poop in the shredder.

1717
01:09:52.520 --> 01:09:57.260
Down in the warehouse, Val enters her office to find Phyllis, Kevin, and Nellie.

1718
01:09:58.020 --> 01:10:02.140
They say, look, we heard you broke up with Daryl, and they really want her to take him

1719
01:10:02.140 --> 01:10:02.580
back.

1720
01:10:03.280 --> 01:10:04.480
And Val's like, you know what?

1721
01:10:04.500 --> 01:10:05.860
I'm going to need you to leave my office.

1722
01:10:05.860 --> 01:10:06.700
Is that all?

1723
01:10:06.900 --> 01:10:09.480
And Nellie's like, no, that's not all.

1724
01:10:09.700 --> 01:10:11.920
And then she has this huge speech.

1725
01:10:12.520 --> 01:10:17.560
Yeah, we got a fan question about it from Nikita C in Sydney, Australia, who said, can

1726
01:10:17.560 --> 01:10:23.060
we talk about Catherine Tate's strange but incredible performance in convincing Val to

1727
01:10:23.060 --> 01:10:24.200
get back with Daryl?

1728
01:10:24.200 --> 01:10:25.980
I agree with you, Nikita.

1729
01:10:26.100 --> 01:10:27.260
We can talk about it.

1730
01:10:27.560 --> 01:10:33.460
I noticed, though, I went to the script because I was curious, that the script is different

1731
01:10:33.460 --> 01:10:35.580
from what ended up in the episode.

1732
01:10:35.800 --> 01:10:37.340
Only by two lines.

1733
01:10:37.520 --> 01:10:37.960
Really?

1734
01:10:38.220 --> 01:10:39.260
Only by two lines.

1735
01:10:39.380 --> 01:10:42.420
Oh, Angela, I was hoping that you would tell me what was up.

1736
01:10:42.580 --> 01:10:42.880
Okay.

1737
01:10:43.100 --> 01:10:45.300
So there were no candy bag alts for this.

1738
01:10:45.400 --> 01:10:45.620
Okay.

1739
01:10:45.820 --> 01:10:47.460
And Catherine really nailed it.

1740
01:10:47.640 --> 01:10:51.820
She delivered it exactly as it was written, except for one part.

1741
01:10:51.820 --> 01:10:56.420
And I don't know if Catherine just forgot in the moment and left out this couplet of dialogue

1742
01:10:56.420 --> 01:10:58.680
or if they decided on the day not to include it.

1743
01:10:59.120 --> 01:11:04.320
But as she does her whole speech, she would have also talked about her countless plastic

1744
01:11:04.320 --> 01:11:09.760
surgeries in which she had a merry-go-round of elective self-abuse.

1745
01:11:10.120 --> 01:11:10.760
Oh, my goodness.

1746
01:11:11.320 --> 01:11:16.080
So I don't know if they decided that that was one too many, but I thought Catherine was

1747
01:11:16.080 --> 01:11:17.260
so great in this moment.

1748
01:11:17.680 --> 01:11:22.560
And I'm just giving shout-outs to all of the Kates and Catherines on our show because I

1749
01:11:22.560 --> 01:11:23.480
think we need to hear it.

1750
01:11:24.320 --> 01:11:24.960
Thank you.

1751
01:11:25.300 --> 01:11:25.960
Is that all?

1752
01:11:26.380 --> 01:11:26.820
No.

1753
01:11:27.080 --> 01:11:28.260
No, that is not all.

1754
01:11:28.660 --> 01:11:30.760
Let me tell you what real life is like.

1755
01:11:31.100 --> 01:11:33.080
The men dry up and the nights get lonely.

1756
01:11:33.540 --> 01:11:37.740
The only calls on your machine are from collection agencies about that pair of motorcycle boots

1757
01:11:37.740 --> 01:11:38.580
you've never even worn.

1758
01:11:38.800 --> 01:11:43.820
You stalk your old high school boyfriend online, go to his daughter's soccer games, and make

1759
01:11:43.820 --> 01:11:44.200
a scene.

1760
01:11:44.380 --> 01:11:49.440
You buy a diamond ring for yourself, wear it on your right hand, and tell yourself you're

1761
01:11:49.440 --> 01:11:50.160
all you need.

1762
01:11:50.380 --> 01:11:55.600
One day, you're alone, tired, at your feet, a dying bird.

1763
01:11:55.980 --> 01:11:57.080
But where did it come from?

1764
01:11:57.400 --> 01:11:58.380
Why did you kill it?

1765
01:11:58.520 --> 01:12:02.120
Is it because in some strange way, it is you?

1766
01:12:03.620 --> 01:12:08.260
Well, if you can believe it, that speech does not sway Val.

1767
01:12:08.720 --> 01:12:10.020
Something else does.

1768
01:12:10.320 --> 01:12:10.960
Shocker.

1769
01:12:11.280 --> 01:12:11.780
Yes.

