01:22:10.760 --> 01:22:11.060
Oh.

2025
01:22:11.240 --> 01:22:13.700
And Brian and I went in May on our own.

2026
01:22:13.860 --> 01:22:15.380
I actually left New York.

2027
01:22:15.520 --> 01:22:19.940
I said, I'm sorry to everyone I served, because I know my pores were real sloppy.

2028
01:22:20.280 --> 01:22:22.100
But it was so much fun.

2029
01:22:22.340 --> 01:22:26.460
There was a local band playing, and it was just such a wonderful night.

2030
01:22:26.580 --> 01:22:30.800
And Brian and I still talk about how special it was.

2031
01:22:30.960 --> 01:22:34.400
I want to give a shout-out to the Scranton mayor at the time, Chris Doherty.

2032
01:22:34.600 --> 01:22:37.380
He was awesome, and the whole town made us feel so welcome.

2033
01:22:37.620 --> 01:22:38.600
That is so cool.

2034
01:22:38.980 --> 01:22:42.980
Well, unfortunately, we didn't get to go to the real Bog to shoot.

2035
01:22:43.460 --> 01:22:49.020
We shot at Tony's Saloon on 7th Street in the Los Angeles Arts District, which is near downtown.

2036
01:22:49.480 --> 01:22:50.360
It's still there.

2037
01:22:50.360 --> 01:22:51.360
You can still go.

2038
01:22:51.940 --> 01:22:55.240
But our producers called the co-owner of the Bog.

2039
01:22:55.440 --> 01:22:56.580
His name is Brian Craig.

2040
01:22:56.840 --> 01:23:01.860
And they told him that Greg would like permission to feature the Bog on the show, asked him to

2041
01:23:01.860 --> 01:23:04.440
film some footage, which he did on his iPhone.

2042
01:23:04.560 --> 01:23:06.120
We tried to make it match.

2043
01:23:06.160 --> 01:23:10.600
And I believe we used that footage for that exterior shot.

2044
01:23:10.800 --> 01:23:11.000
Yes.

2045
01:23:11.000 --> 01:23:12.380
That's a real exterior.

2046
01:23:12.800 --> 01:23:17.340
And speaking of pouring drinks, Angela, fan question from Emily P.

2047
01:23:17.560 --> 01:23:18.880
in Nashua, New Hampshire,

2048
01:23:19.440 --> 01:23:20.420
said this.

2049
01:23:21.100 --> 01:23:27.160
I hope there is a fan mail flurry about the way Pam pours beer, because it makes me so mad.

2050
01:23:27.340 --> 01:23:33.180
If she did that to me, I would ask her to buy me a new beer that isn't poured into foam land.

2051
01:23:33.380 --> 01:23:34.420
Did you notice this?

2052
01:23:34.520 --> 01:23:35.220
I noticed it.

2053
01:23:35.220 --> 01:23:37.220
Can you read what I printed in blue?

2054
01:23:37.900 --> 01:23:38.880
Read out loud.

2055
01:23:39.580 --> 01:23:41.720
Read out loud what I wrote in my document.

2056
01:23:43.140 --> 01:23:46.600
You wrote, Pam does not know how to pour beer.

2057
01:23:48.160 --> 01:23:50.100
You guys, I don't drink beer.

2058
01:23:50.100 --> 01:23:50.740
Is it obvious?

2059
01:23:51.260 --> 01:23:51.700
Yes.

2060
01:23:51.900 --> 01:23:53.280
No one wants all that foam.

2061
01:23:53.460 --> 01:23:54.840
You have to tilt the glass.

2062
01:23:54.860 --> 01:23:55.220
I know.

2063
01:23:55.300 --> 01:23:55.960
Tilt the pitcher.

2064
01:23:55.980 --> 01:23:56.900
I mean, I don't know.

2065
01:23:57.080 --> 01:23:58.020
No, you don't know.

2066
01:23:58.020 --> 01:24:01.800
We were drinking Phil's special non-alcoholic beer.

2067
01:24:02.020 --> 01:24:05.280
It foams up just like real beer, and I clearly did not know what I was doing.

2068
01:24:06.760 --> 01:24:09.640
Well, Pam and Meredith are really bonding.

2069
01:24:09.980 --> 01:24:14.080
I just loved doing these scenes with Kate.

2070
01:24:14.220 --> 01:24:16.860
We got to spend a whole evening together, just the two of us.

2071
01:24:17.400 --> 01:24:21.820
You know, Pam says she has a newfound respect for Meredith's life as a single mother.

2072
01:24:22.320 --> 01:24:26.880
Pam also compliments Meredith's new bald head, says, you know, you're really rocking it.

2073
01:24:26.880 --> 01:24:27.460
You look good.

2074
01:24:27.580 --> 01:24:28.380
You're pulling it off.

2075
01:24:28.520 --> 01:24:32.180
And Meredith says, oh, yeah, I already got the bartender's number.

2076
01:24:32.780 --> 01:24:32.980
Yeah.

2077
01:24:33.460 --> 01:24:35.040
Things are going to happen later.

2078
01:24:35.200 --> 01:24:35.400
Yeah.

2079
01:24:35.600 --> 01:24:37.060
She's going to take him to Bone Town.

2080
01:24:37.260 --> 01:24:37.840
That's right.

2081
01:24:38.400 --> 01:24:42.300
This scene was longer in the shooting draft, and I loved it so much.

2082
01:24:42.760 --> 01:24:47.220
Meredith is going to try to give Pam some words of wisdom about solo parenting.

2083
01:24:47.440 --> 01:24:49.220
I remember this so well.

2084
01:24:49.380 --> 01:24:50.400
I have to share it.

2085
01:24:50.480 --> 01:24:50.960
Please do.

2086
01:24:51.200 --> 01:24:52.820
This is how it read in the shooting draft.

2087
01:24:53.340 --> 01:24:54.820
Meredith, here's a tip.

2088
01:24:55.100 --> 01:24:56.780
Screw around all you want.

2089
01:24:56.880 --> 01:24:59.100
But don't bring a guy into your child's home.

2090
01:24:59.400 --> 01:25:02.540
In a pinch, use the garage or do him on the porch.

2091
01:25:03.280 --> 01:25:04.160
The porch.

2092
01:25:05.120 --> 01:25:09.000
Meredith says, what I'm saying is, be a good mom to your kids firSt.

2093
01:25:09.320 --> 01:25:12.100
Pam says, well, of course, I would never screw around.

2094
01:25:12.280 --> 01:25:13.960
And Meredith goes, I don't judge.

2095
01:25:14.180 --> 01:25:15.360
Life is to be enjoyed.

2096
01:25:15.700 --> 01:25:17.080
Have a Crisco party.

2097
01:25:17.400 --> 01:25:18.720
Get it on with the prieSt.

2098
01:25:18.900 --> 01:25:20.900
Pam goes, I would not do that.

2099
01:25:21.720 --> 01:25:24.800
Meredith says, but the kids come firSt.

2100
01:25:25.340 --> 01:25:26.200
That's sacred.

2101
01:25:26.500 --> 01:25:27.580
You know what I'm talking about?

2102
01:25:27.940 --> 01:25:30.280
Pam says, I get the gist of it.

2103
01:25:30.680 --> 01:25:34.680
Meredith says, dress up like a jockey and do the Penn State lacrosse team.

2104
01:25:34.840 --> 01:25:36.300
I don't care.

2105
01:25:36.300 --> 01:25:38.900
But first, the kids.

2106
01:25:39.260 --> 01:25:42.040
Pam takes a swig of beer and burps.

2107
01:25:42.320 --> 01:25:44.200
Meredith says, there you go.

2108
01:25:44.340 --> 01:25:45.580
And they clink glasses.

2109
01:25:46.600 --> 01:25:49.240
The kids come firSt.

2110
01:25:49.240 --> 01:26:00.460
I remember that runner because I remember there were some alts that she would just throw out like one ridiculous escapade after another, but then be like, but the kids come firSt.

2111
01:26:01.240 --> 01:26:01.480
Yes.

2112
01:26:01.880 --> 01:26:06.960
Well, this scene ends with a fantastic karaoke moment with Pam and Meredith.

2113
01:26:07.220 --> 01:26:09.200
They're going to sing Girls Just Want to Have Fun.

2114
01:26:09.400 --> 01:26:11.120
I absolutely loved it.

2115
01:26:11.320 --> 01:26:12.140
Oh, my goodness.

2116
01:26:12.140 --> 01:26:14.100
We got a fan letter from Martha B.

2117
01:26:14.160 --> 01:26:21.320
in Malta who said, the karaoke to Girls Just Want to Have Fun is peak girlhood and a really nice way to end this episode.

2118
01:26:21.940 --> 01:26:27.520
Question is, the part where Meredith starts early, was that scripted or did it actually happen?

2119
01:26:28.220 --> 01:26:35.180
Well, Martha, we asked Kate about doing this scene and she actually answered your question.

2120
01:26:35.540 --> 01:26:37.020
Here's what she had to say.

2121
01:26:37.720 --> 01:26:40.920
That was like one of my most favorite scenes ever.

2122
01:26:41.160 --> 01:26:45.400
I got to sing karaoke and I actually sing, but I was told Meredith doesn't sing.

2123
01:26:45.660 --> 01:26:48.620
So when I sang, whenever Meredith sang, she wasn't supposed to be good.

2124
01:26:48.760 --> 01:26:51.300
So it was really fun just to get to sing.

2125
01:26:51.420 --> 01:26:52.960
And we sang Girls Just Want to Have Fun.

2126
01:26:53.060 --> 01:26:58.560
And I just remember we had this improvised moment where I literally started too soon.

2127
01:26:58.860 --> 01:27:00.940
And Pam looks at Meredith and is like, not yet.

2128
01:27:01.140 --> 01:27:03.720
Like, it was so perfectly timed, her cutting me off.

2129
01:27:03.900 --> 01:27:04.240
It was so funny.

2130
01:27:04.380 --> 01:27:05.340
It was a totally improvised moment.

2131
01:27:05.460 --> 01:27:05.920
They kept it in.

2132
01:27:05.920 --> 01:27:08.120
And yeah, way to go, Jenna.

2133
01:27:09.320 --> 01:27:10.520
That was perfect.

2134
01:27:10.520 --> 01:27:12.460
I didn't realize that was improvised.

2135
01:27:12.660 --> 01:27:12.860
Yeah.

2136
01:27:13.280 --> 01:27:13.520
Yeah.

2137
01:27:13.680 --> 01:27:14.460
It was so fun.

2138
01:27:15.040 --> 01:27:16.640
And I didn't want to stop singing.

2139
01:27:16.880 --> 01:27:18.140
We were like, can we do one more?

2140
01:27:18.240 --> 01:27:19.340
We think we should do one more.

2141
01:27:19.500 --> 01:27:20.680
And they were like, we got it.

2142
01:27:20.740 --> 01:27:21.300
We got it.

2143
01:27:21.340 --> 01:27:21.960
We're like, no, no, no.

2144
01:27:22.020 --> 01:27:22.940
We could do one more.

2145
01:27:23.540 --> 01:27:27.760
It reminds me of that moment when Steve and Tim Meadows were improvising that baby back,

2146
01:27:27.860 --> 01:27:28.140
baby back.

2147
01:27:28.160 --> 01:27:28.400
Yeah, yeah.

2148
01:27:28.560 --> 01:27:29.300
And Steve's like, no, no, no.

2149
01:27:29.620 --> 01:27:29.940
Yeah.

2150
01:27:30.440 --> 01:27:31.580
It's the same idea.

2151
01:27:31.780 --> 01:27:32.340
It was great.

2152
01:27:32.600 --> 01:27:32.900
Totally.

2153
01:27:33.680 --> 01:27:33.920
Oh.

2154
01:27:33.920 --> 01:27:36.140
Well, everyone, that was nice.

2155
01:27:36.440 --> 01:27:40.280
A huge thank you to Steve Burgess and to Kate Flannery.

2156
01:27:40.280 --> 01:27:45.400
Yes, and to Jeff Hatch, the limo driver, for sharing with us their behind-the-scenes moments

2157
01:27:45.400 --> 01:27:46.200
of this episode.

2158
01:27:46.520 --> 01:27:50.100
Big thank you to you all for writing in your questions and your comments.

2159
01:27:50.260 --> 01:27:51.260
You know we love them.

2160
01:27:51.420 --> 01:27:55.300
Thank you, Cassie, Jordan, and Angela, for my wonderful birthday celebration.

2161
01:27:55.300 --> 01:27:59.820
And thank you to everybody out there for listening to all my tangents today.

2162
01:28:00.200 --> 01:28:07.700
I heard from Cody that there is a stack of birthday cards waiting for me at SiriusXM.

2163
01:28:07.860 --> 01:28:09.080
They're going to get them to me.

2164
01:28:09.280 --> 01:28:10.420
Thank you so much.

2165
01:28:10.420 --> 01:28:11.280
Oh, my gosh.

2166
01:28:11.360 --> 01:28:13.380
You guys really know how to celebrate a person.

2167
01:28:13.620 --> 01:28:14.600
Y'all are the beSt.

2168
01:28:14.600 --> 01:28:20.600
And I really feel like we have to go out on Girls Just Want to Have Fun by Pam and Meredith.

2169
01:28:20.840 --> 01:28:21.280
For sure.

2170
01:28:21.500 --> 01:28:22.940
We'll see you next week, everyone.

2171
01:28:22.940 --> 01:28:32.700
Not yet.

2172
01:28:58.220 --> 01:29:00.180
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.

2173
01:29:00.480 --> 01:29:04.600
Office Ladies is produced by Earwolf, Jenna Fisher, and Angela Kinsey.

2174
01:29:04.780 --> 01:29:07.100
Our senior producer is Cassie Jerkins.

2175
01:29:07.300 --> 01:29:09.380
Our audio engineer is Jordan Duffy.

2176
01:29:09.640 --> 01:29:11.820
And our associate producer is Ainsley Bubaco.

2177
01:29:12.140 --> 01:29:15.080
Our theme song is Rubber Tree by Creed Bratton.
